WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:01:47.835 --> 00:01:50.005
When I was little,


00:01:50.175 --> 00:01:54.715
my mom and I loved to sit
and look at the night sky.


00:01:56.135 --> 00:01:58.255
We dreamed that we were not alone,


00:02:00.545 --> 00:02:03.425
that the stars were
the eyes of the angels


00:02:03.595 --> 00:02:05.635
who were watching over us.


00:02:07.005 --> 00:02:11.295
But when mom fell ill,
none of them helped.


00:02:12.885 --> 00:02:15.835
And so I realized that
there's nothing out there,


00:02:17.345 --> 00:02:22.795
except silence, emptiness and cold.


00:02:23.465 --> 00:02:24.885
Let's go.


00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.425
Quiet!


00:02:26.595 --> 00:02:29.505
Charl, what are you looking at?
There's nothing there.


00:02:29.675 --> 00:02:30.925
Come on, let's go!


00:03:50.004 --> 00:03:53.634
For most of history, people
have feared meteor showers.


00:03:54.134 --> 00:03:57.464
Only recently have we begun
to understand these visitors


00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.924
who penetrates the Earth's atmosphere.


00:04:00.094 --> 00:04:05.754
Earlier on, these cosmic stones were
associated with the wrath of God.


00:04:05.924 --> 00:04:07.544
How are things with you?


00:04:08.344 --> 00:04:10.084
Why don't you tell me?


00:04:10.254 --> 00:04:13.833
I'll get together with some Albert,
and won't tell a thing about it.


00:04:14.003 --> 00:04:16.673
- There's nothing to tell.
- Nothing, really?


00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.213
What's going on between you two?
Where do you... you know?


00:04:20.383 --> 00:04:24.753
If I knew such a Romeo,
I'd run away from home.


00:04:24.923 --> 00:04:25.923
Maybe.


00:04:26.093 --> 00:04:30.833
But Tyoma thinks of Romeo only as
a make of car, if you see what I mean.


00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:36.083
And today we are witnessing a
unique astronomical phenomenon.


00:04:36.713 --> 00:04:38.383
Mironov...


00:04:39.093 --> 00:04:41.023
Good morning.
Did you sleep well?


00:04:41.093 --> 00:04:43.333
- Why Mironov?
- Just because. Don't sleep!


00:04:43.503 --> 00:04:44.633
Who can tell me


00:04:44.793 --> 00:04:46.963
where and when occurred
the last meteor shower,


00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:50.463
that had a magnitude comparable to
what's expected today.


00:04:51.093 --> 00:04:52.673
In China.


00:04:52.833 --> 00:04:53.963
'76.


00:04:54.753 --> 00:04:58.213
Yulia. Are you having a
scientific debate?


00:04:58.383 --> 00:05:01.043
- A scientific debate, exactly.
- And?


00:05:01.213 --> 00:05:05.213
Google says in China, in 1976.


00:05:05.633 --> 00:05:06.753
Google is right.


00:05:06.923 --> 00:05:09.463
The most terrible events in
human history


00:05:09.633 --> 00:05:12.243
have happened when men
faced something...


00:05:12.473 --> 00:05:13.543
Unknown...


00:05:14.543 --> 00:05:15.633
Frightening.


00:05:15.633 --> 00:05:19.843
The bloodiest crusades were
triggered by meteor showers.


00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:23.463
And then what happened, Mironov?!


00:05:24.753 --> 00:05:26.883
I'm not sleeping, I'm listening.


00:05:27.043 --> 00:05:28.213
Google.


00:05:28.923 --> 00:05:32.463
All the crusaders, about 300,000
people, died in the desert.


00:05:32.883 --> 00:05:34.043
Yes. Yes.


00:05:34.213 --> 00:05:35.423
The brain!


00:05:35.503 --> 00:05:37.783
And this despite the fact that


00:05:37.833 --> 00:05:40.613
these meteor showers, in scale,
don't compare with today's.


00:05:40.623 --> 00:05:42.993
And us here... won't we also...?


00:05:44.173 --> 00:05:45.583
Are you crazy?


00:05:50.132 --> 00:05:51.422
I hope not.


00:05:52.042 --> 00:05:55.542
The debris will burn up in the upper
atmosphere, don't be afraid.


00:05:55.712 --> 00:05:57.632
Tonight, watch the shooting stars!


00:05:57.792 --> 00:05:58.542
Did you hear?


00:05:58.712 --> 00:06:00.212
- Yes!
- Take care!


00:06:00.382 --> 00:06:01.462
By the way...


00:06:02.632 --> 00:06:04.542
- What's this?
- Two concert tickets for Korzh.


00:06:04.712 --> 00:06:06.422
I thought you and I could go.


00:06:06.592 --> 00:06:09.752
But compared to your
Alfa Romeo's vroom vroom,


00:06:09.922 --> 00:06:12.132
I'm not really in the race.
- Thank you!


00:06:12.292 --> 00:06:13.582
- Bye!
- Bye!


00:06:13.752 --> 00:06:14.962
All the best!
The shooting stars tonight!


00:06:15.132 --> 00:06:17.002
- Yes! - Bye!
- Bye!


00:06:29.342 --> 00:06:32.882
- Give me your notebook, I'll correct it.
- Were you a good student?


00:06:36.132 --> 00:06:37.922
I'll call you.


00:06:41.462 --> 00:06:42.462
Hi.


00:06:44.672 --> 00:06:45.672
Well then...


00:06:55.462 --> 00:06:56.462
Dad?


00:06:57.462 --> 00:06:58.922
Hi! It's me.


00:06:59.092 --> 00:07:00.792
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:07:03.002 --> 00:07:04.672
I'm home just for a few seconds.


00:07:06.462 --> 00:07:08.422
Do you know where
the binoculars are?


00:07:08.592 --> 00:07:10.172
I'll be home late tonight.


00:07:10.342 --> 00:07:11.832
Don't leave the apartment.


00:07:12.002 --> 00:07:14.382
But we're all meeting at
the parking lot.


00:07:14.542 --> 00:07:16.832
- It's the best spot to see the meteors.
- No.


00:07:18.832 --> 00:07:21.132
Definitely no?


00:07:21.292 --> 00:07:23.542
Is there any weighty arguments?


00:07:23.712 --> 00:07:25.381
Convincing reasons?


00:07:25.541 --> 00:07:28.671
Crowds of people on a
roof with a low wall,


00:07:28.831 --> 00:07:30.881
most of them drunk.


00:07:32.091 --> 00:07:34.501
I think the argument is convincing.


00:07:35.751 --> 00:07:38.581
Dad, I won't be alone.
Tyoma is waiting for me.


00:07:39.341 --> 00:07:41.081
- Artyom?
- Yes.


00:07:42.831 --> 00:07:44.171
Then, certainly, no!


00:07:49.631 --> 00:07:50.881
Great!


00:07:51.041 --> 00:07:52.881
I don't mean to pressure you, but


00:07:53.041 --> 00:07:56.291
a meteor shower like that won't
occur again for maybe 50 years.


00:07:56.461 --> 00:07:57.671
I'm not coming.


00:07:59.671 --> 00:08:02.831
- Did Comrade Colonel forbid you to go out?
- He never leaves me alone!


00:08:03.001 --> 00:08:06.131
I wish they'd sent him somewhere.
On a business trip.


00:08:06.291 --> 00:08:07.291
To Jupiter!


00:08:09.091 --> 00:08:11.581
He just left. I saw him.


00:08:11.751 --> 00:08:14.081
So, I see no problem.


00:08:14.251 --> 00:08:16.461
I'm ready to rescue my
princess from the tower.


00:08:42.671 --> 00:08:44.461
Unidentified flying object detected.


00:08:44.631 --> 00:08:47.501
Bearing 340, distance 280.


00:08:47.671 --> 00:08:50.001
The flying object doesn't answer.


00:08:51.461 --> 00:08:55.001
The object came from the west.
It's now just north of Finland.


00:08:56.341 --> 00:08:59.291
- What kind of object?
- It was just detected.


00:09:00.791 --> 00:09:02.830
Very large, moves in our direction.


00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.790
- Roger that.
- Speed?


00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:10.670
- Speed is erratic.
- Erratic? Are they in trouble?


00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:14.330
Not yet ascertained.
It moves at between 500 and 900 km/h.


00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.620
- Strategic partners were consulted?
- Yes! They don't know.


00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.780
Lithuania and Latvia
are also on standby.


00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:23.250
But if this thing doesn't slow down,
they won't even have time to take off.


00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:27.210
<i>Bearing 190.
The object has passed the coast.</i>


00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:30.790
<i>It's big. Keeping visual contact.</i>


00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:35.000
Deploy interceptors.
Activate missile defence.


00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:37.750
Notify the Ministry and let them
announce the state of emergency.


00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:52.230
<i>Ready!</i>


00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:55.040
<i>477 is in the air!</i>


00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:57.170
477 to Atlanta, I'm on my way.


00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:03.630
<i>477 and 478 are on course.</i>


00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.630
Despite the high-rise buildings,
we have a good view of the sky.


00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:14.210
And there's much to see today!


00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.000
The north-east of the capital is cloudy,


00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:18.830
<i>so many came here, south of Moscow,</i>


00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.580
<i>to watch this celestial show.</i>


00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:24.710
Don't listen to this drivel!


00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:30.170
Fuck off!


00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:38.709
<i>As you can see, some are already beginning
to celebrate this rare natural event...</i>


00:10:38.879 --> 00:10:40.539
<i>Crap! Let's do it again!</i>


00:10:40.709 --> 00:10:41.829
Leave it!


00:10:41.999 --> 00:10:44.629
I'm just going to adjust his mirrors.


00:10:49.999 --> 00:10:51.749
Hey, what's that bullshit?!


00:10:53.089 --> 00:10:55.379
There are pedestrians around here!


00:10:57.669 --> 00:10:59.539
What the hell?!


00:11:00.589 --> 00:11:02.039
Do you need help, Tyoma?


00:11:09.089 --> 00:11:11.329
All right, guys.


00:11:11.499 --> 00:11:13.379
There's no need!


00:11:14.829 --> 00:11:16.039
Hi!


00:11:17.209 --> 00:11:19.709
- Guess what I got.
- What's this?


00:11:19.879 --> 00:11:22.129
A ticket for the VIP box!


00:11:25.169 --> 00:11:26.499
<i>477. 10 on the left.</i>


00:11:26.919 --> 00:11:29.209
Roger that. Have visual contact.


00:11:33.289 --> 00:11:35.169
This is crazy!


00:11:35.339 --> 00:11:37.459
Repeat, 477.


00:11:37.709 --> 00:11:39.629
<i>It's huge!</i>


00:11:45.339 --> 00:11:47.329
- Yulia.
- Yes?


00:11:47.499 --> 00:11:49.169
I think we're in the way.


00:11:49.709 --> 00:11:50.959
- We?
- We!


00:11:51.129 --> 00:11:53.709
Don't you see she wants to be alone?


00:11:54.289 --> 00:11:55.919
- Uh, no.
- Yes.


00:11:56.089 --> 00:11:58.819
She's my friend and
I'm not leaving her alone.


00:12:01.959 --> 00:12:05.599
Take it! You're so annoying!
Go. No one's there. I live alone.


00:12:05.669 --> 00:12:07.039
Oh what a beauty!


00:12:07.209 --> 00:12:10.209
"Oh what a beauty!"
You have no idea what's beautiful!


00:12:10.379 --> 00:12:11.879
You'll miss this.


00:12:12.039 --> 00:12:14.129
We're in a Moscow inner courtyard,


00:12:14.289 --> 00:12:16.748
and right behind me, you
can see the meteor shower.


00:12:17.168 --> 00:12:18.708
Show me another one.


00:12:19.378 --> 00:12:20.378
Yes.


00:12:34.458 --> 00:12:37.458
Be quiet!
Wait, wait, wait, wait!


00:12:50.418 --> 00:12:53.018
<i>Base to 477. The aim is to disable it.</i>


00:12:53.088 --> 00:12:55.128
<i>477 to base. I hear you.</i>


00:12:55.288 --> 00:12:57.958
<i>477, fire then bank to the left.</i>


00:13:00.418 --> 00:13:05.248
- And if it's not NATO?
- How could it not? See any force field?


00:13:13.958 --> 00:13:16.038
<i>477, was the target hit?</i>


00:13:21.128 --> 00:13:24.288
<i>Yup! It's losing speed.</i>


00:13:26.498 --> 00:13:28.668
<i>477 to base. I'm losing control!</i>


00:13:29.128 --> 00:13:30.998
<i>477, self-eject!</i>


00:13:36.958 --> 00:13:39.458
Sveta stayed there alone.
I can't do this.


00:13:39.628 --> 00:13:41.748
She's your friend, she can wait.


00:13:42.918 --> 00:13:46.418
Can I at least call her briefly?
Please, Tyoma!


00:15:19.997 --> 00:15:22.377
Yulia! Hold tight!


00:15:51.746 --> 00:15:53.496
Hold tight!


00:16:30.496 --> 00:16:32.666
Intelligence is almost there.


00:16:32.826 --> 00:16:35.076
They should report in a few minutes.


00:16:35.246 --> 00:16:37.246
The Tech unit is also on its way.


00:16:37.416 --> 00:16:39.536
- Do you hear me?
- Yes I'm listening.


00:16:39.706 --> 00:16:41.806
- Protective clothing, Colonel.
- I don't need it.


00:16:41.876 --> 00:16:43.496
Be careful.


00:16:43.666 --> 00:16:46.666
You understand,
who knows what this thing is?


00:16:47.286 --> 00:16:49.416
And here's another great news.


00:16:49.586 --> 00:16:52.266
A deputy from the parliamentary
group is going with you.


00:16:52.336 --> 00:16:54.626
- What's that about?
- It's necessary.


00:16:55.746 --> 00:16:57.786
He wants to see the impact zone.


00:16:57.956 --> 00:17:00.956
Is this really XL?
Yes, it's wide enough.


00:17:23.915 --> 00:17:25.855
The world's attention is riveted


00:17:25.925 --> 00:17:28.215
on the events unfolding in Moscow.


00:17:28.285 --> 00:17:31.875
We managed to get through to
Mikhail Poleskin, State Duma deputy,


00:17:31.935 --> 00:17:34.855
who plans to personally inspect
the scene of the crash.


00:17:34.925 --> 00:17:37.755
Mikhail Petrovich, where are
you and what has happened?


00:17:37.825 --> 00:17:40.695
<i>At the moment, I am stillte.</i>


00:17:40.765 --> 00:17:42.765
There is no reason to claim that


00:17:42.825 --> 00:17:45.915
we're dealing here with an
object of extraterrestrial origin.


00:17:46.085 --> 00:17:48.535
But if this assumption
were confirmed,


00:17:48.705 --> 00:17:51.615
this event would certainly
go down in history.


00:17:54.995 --> 00:17:57.825
17 teams are already on the ground
and 4 are close to Chertanovo.


00:17:57.995 --> 00:18:01.575
- One is on the road with dogs.
- Mobilize all reservists!


00:18:06.535 --> 00:18:08.205
Take the girl!


00:18:12.585 --> 00:18:13.575
Yulia!


00:18:14.125 --> 00:18:16.165
Yulia, look at me!


00:18:16.335 --> 00:18:17.325
Yulia!


00:18:17.875 --> 00:18:19.285
Stop!


00:18:21.085 --> 00:18:23.915
- Are you tired of life?!
- Open the door, quickly!


00:18:25.415 --> 00:18:26.415
Yulia!


00:18:26.585 --> 00:18:29.285
Do you hear me? Stay with me!


00:18:29.995 --> 00:18:32.125
- Come on, come on!
- Carefully!


00:18:39.375 --> 00:18:42.914
Of course, it's not safe. You never
know what's inside this thing.


00:18:43.084 --> 00:18:47.374
There could be a nuclear reactor
and a second Chernobyl awaiting us.


00:18:47.534 --> 00:18:51.244
Why did they chose you for contact?
Was this a committee decision?


00:18:51.414 --> 00:18:55.664
No, I volunteered and the
Ministry of Defence agreed.


00:18:56.664 --> 00:18:58.244
Hello? Can you hear me?


00:18:58.624 --> 00:19:00.744
Did you activate the jammers already?


00:19:00.914 --> 00:19:03.324
- Can you stop where there's reception?
- No.


00:19:04.164 --> 00:19:05.704
But it's a live broadcast!


00:19:05.874 --> 00:19:08.034
Mikhail Petrovich, can you hear us?


00:19:09.124 --> 00:19:11.044
Unfortunately, we lost the connection.


00:19:11.414 --> 00:19:14.134
Let me remind you that, about an hour ago,


00:19:14.134 --> 00:19:16.964
a catastrophic incident occurred
in Chertanovo.


00:19:16.964 --> 00:19:20.914
An unidentified object crashed
in a residential tower complex.


00:19:20.914 --> 00:19:23.734
The number of victims is yet
to be determined.


00:19:23.804 --> 00:19:26.764
The Atlantic Alliance is currently
negotiating with Moscow


00:19:26.764 --> 00:19:28.264
for access to the site.


00:19:28.274 --> 00:19:31.354
Experts are reluctant to confirm
the reports of eye-witnesses


00:19:31.424 --> 00:19:34.844
to the effect that we're dealing
with an alien invasion.


00:19:34.914 --> 00:19:37.524
And yet, from different parts of the world


00:19:37.594 --> 00:19:40.724
come reports of armed forces
on high state of alert.


00:19:41.284 --> 00:19:45.144
Meanwhile, the streets adjacent to
the crash site are cordoned off.


00:19:45.214 --> 00:19:48.054
The Defence Ministry is so far
abstaining from comment.


00:19:48.124 --> 00:19:52.204
But local residents tell of tactical units
surrounding a strange sphere.


00:19:52.374 --> 00:19:55.874
Combat helicopters are also
hovering over the crashed object.


00:20:01.584 --> 00:20:04.704
<i>- What about radioactivity?
- In the normal range.</i>


00:20:04.874 --> 00:20:07.704
<i>There is no danger for people. Over.</i>


00:20:08.414 --> 00:20:10.204
<i>We'll keep monitoring. Over.</i>


00:20:13.874 --> 00:20:15.874
I'm in position. Everything's quiet.


00:20:16.624 --> 00:20:18.873
- Any visible activity?
- Nothing to see.


00:20:37.163 --> 00:20:38.473
We have contact.


00:20:39.413 --> 00:20:40.413
I see it.


00:20:40.583 --> 00:20:42.123
<i>The object is in my sight.</i>


00:20:42.283 --> 00:20:45.663
Well, it's time for
a welcome speech.


00:20:53.533 --> 00:20:55.243
I greet you.


00:20:59.743 --> 00:21:01.703
I'm Michael Poleskin,


00:21:01.873 --> 00:21:04.203
the member of Parliament.


00:21:05.663 --> 00:21:07.953
This is the representative
of the Ministry of Defence,


00:21:08.123 --> 00:21:12.033
responsible for the sector, so to speak...
Lebedev.


00:21:12.743 --> 00:21:15.073
Your name's Lebedev?
- Lebedev.


00:21:15.823 --> 00:21:19.473
We are ready for fruitful cooperation.


00:21:20.233 --> 00:21:23.593
<i>The first step to which
has already been laid</i>


00:21:23.793 --> 00:21:27.623
in the course of our contribution
to your successful landing.


00:21:27.663 --> 00:21:29.163
So...


00:21:29.333 --> 00:21:30.913
Welcome to our Earth!


00:21:31.083 --> 00:21:32.283
Don't.


00:21:32.453 --> 00:21:34.413
No abrupt movements.


00:21:44.163 --> 00:21:46.703
<i>We got that. fire.</i>


00:21:46.873 --> 00:21:49.073
<i>- Negative!
- Roger that.</i>


00:21:56.872 --> 00:21:59.652
Report every detail. Subjectively.


00:21:59.782 --> 00:22:02.622
What you saw, felt, thought.


00:22:02.782 --> 00:22:07.032
They asked us not to come nearer.
They said we could avoid casualties,


00:22:07.202 --> 00:22:11.032
if we let them repair their
ship and leave our planet.


00:22:11.202 --> 00:22:13.372
What do you mean by "said"?
With words?


00:22:13.532 --> 00:22:16.952
- I'm not sure, but I understood.
- In what language did you speak?


00:22:17.952 --> 00:22:18.952
In Russian.


00:22:19.122 --> 00:22:22.162
What did they mean by "avoid casualties"?
Was that a threat?


00:22:22.332 --> 00:22:24.382
I don't think so.
I didn't sense aggression.


00:22:24.452 --> 00:22:26.242
Has anyone else heard
this conversation?


00:22:26.412 --> 00:22:28.992
- A deputy was with you.
- Yes. He's in intensive care.


00:22:28.992 --> 00:22:31.872
His pacemaker failed. Like all electronic
devices near the ship.


00:22:31.912 --> 00:22:36.162
I'm sorry, but what's stopping us
from carrying out an assault right now?


00:22:36.332 --> 00:22:39.862
I agree. We shot them down somehow,
so liquidation shouldn't be a problem...


00:22:39.922 --> 00:22:43.302
If we hadn't shot them down,
there wouldn't have been any victims.


00:22:43.822 --> 00:22:45.622
What do you suggest?


00:22:46.282 --> 00:22:49.072
Wait. Keep observing them.
Nothing more.


00:22:49.242 --> 00:22:52.032
The main thing now is
not to provoke aggression.


00:22:56.222 --> 00:22:57.352
Let's wait.


00:22:59.242 --> 00:23:01.002
For 3 days, the world's attention


00:23:01.002 --> 00:23:03.242
have been riveted on
the events in Moscow.


00:23:03.242 --> 00:23:07.052
The object is being examined by an
international group of experts.


00:23:07.052 --> 00:23:10.992
The UN Security Council has raised
concerns about the Moscow incident.


00:23:11.262 --> 00:23:16.732
A US government representative has demanded
immediate access to the crash site.


00:23:16.802 --> 00:23:20.122
The UN resolution however
was blocked by the Russian side.


00:23:28.582 --> 00:23:29.991
Woke up?


00:23:37.031 --> 00:23:39.031
- Yulia?
- Oh, hi.


00:23:39.451 --> 00:23:41.741
- How are you?
- My head hurts.


00:23:41.911 --> 00:23:43.951
Yeah... So, Yulia.


00:23:44.911 --> 00:23:45.911
Look here.


00:23:50.281 --> 00:23:51.281
Good.


00:23:52.531 --> 00:23:54.661
You shouldn't have taken
off the bandage.


00:23:54.821 --> 00:23:57.031
Lie down. I'll call your father.


00:23:57.201 --> 00:24:00.821
... Commander Lebedev is responsible for
the coordination of the armed forces.


00:24:00.991 --> 00:24:04.871
Within a radius of 1 km, protective
structures have been erected.


00:24:05.031 --> 00:24:07.621
The nearby streets are
closed to traffic,


00:24:07.781 --> 00:24:09.241
the residents have been evacuated


00:24:09.241 --> 00:24:11.871
although many have refused
to leave, fearing looting.


00:24:12.041 --> 00:24:15.941
The death tolls now stands at 232.
Dozens are listed as missing.


00:24:16.821 --> 00:24:18.411
Sveta...


00:24:44.201 --> 00:24:45.281
Tyoma.


00:24:46.991 --> 00:24:49.491
Did the doctor allow you to get up?


00:24:50.081 --> 00:24:51.371
Look at this.


00:25:24.410 --> 00:25:26.160
My little one, what is it?


00:25:26.330 --> 00:25:28.740
I'm with you! I'll always
be there, do you hear?


00:25:43.990 --> 00:25:44.990
Hop in!


00:25:47.620 --> 00:25:49.280
Thanks, Tyoma!


00:25:54.740 --> 00:25:56.570
Andrei, I'm driving!


00:25:56.670 --> 00:26:00.400
The doctor said she's OK, but
if her head starts spinning or hurting,


00:26:00.400 --> 00:26:03.190
- to come back at once.
- Thank you for taking her here.


00:26:03.620 --> 00:26:05.490
But without you...


00:26:06.030 --> 00:26:07.870
she wouldn't have been there.


00:26:10.370 --> 00:26:11.910
You're welcome.


00:26:29.580 --> 00:26:32.950
<i>... has rejected the proposal on the
participation of international experts</i>


00:26:33.120 --> 00:26:36.030
<i>in the study of the
crashed object in Moscow.</i>


00:26:36.200 --> 00:26:39.370
<i>The Russian president has
emphasized that our own experts</i>


00:26:39.440 --> 00:26:42.320
<i>have the skills and
technical equipment required</i>


00:26:42.490 --> 00:26:44.119
<i>to monitor the situation.</i>


00:26:44.189 --> 00:26:47.269
<i>The government spokesman has
stressed that today's talk</i>


00:26:47.329 --> 00:26:49.819
<i>occurred at the request of
the American side.</i>


00:26:59.709 --> 00:27:03.289
<i>In further news, more than
200 deaths have been reported.</i>


00:27:04.119 --> 00:27:06.419
The news said 200 people died.


00:27:07.159 --> 00:27:08.869
Is it true or a lie?


00:27:09.029 --> 00:27:10.199
It's true.


00:27:12.989 --> 00:27:14.489
Are we at war, or what?


00:27:14.819 --> 00:27:17.869
Depends on how they behave.


00:27:19.909 --> 00:27:21.699
Who are they?


00:27:23.909 --> 00:27:25.239
That's a good question.


00:27:30.239 --> 00:27:32.449
THIS IS OUR EARTH!


00:27:41.279 --> 00:27:43.069
Dad?


00:27:43.239 --> 00:27:45.199
What will happen to us now?


00:27:45.369 --> 00:27:48.589
The city is under curfew. No
one is allowed out after 9pm.


00:27:48.659 --> 00:27:51.489
You come home immediately
after school. Is that clear?


00:27:52.619 --> 00:27:53.659
Yes sir!


00:27:53.819 --> 00:27:56.659
You know, Yulia, I've got
enough to do at the moment.


00:27:56.819 --> 00:27:58.659
I cannot watch you all the time.


00:27:58.819 --> 00:28:02.199
Can you, for once in your
life, help me? Just help me?!


00:28:03.489 --> 00:28:04.869
You're welcome.


00:28:34.738 --> 00:28:36.448
Well finally!


00:28:36.618 --> 00:28:38.068
- Good day.
- Hi.


00:28:38.238 --> 00:28:39.488
Hi grandma!


00:28:39.658 --> 00:28:41.738
How many times have I asked you?


00:28:41.908 --> 00:28:44.988
Just say Ljuba.
I don't like that word.


00:28:45.158 --> 00:28:46.658
How are you, sweety?


00:28:46.818 --> 00:28:49.318
He got you here, did he not,
so I wouldn't run away?


00:28:49.488 --> 00:28:52.158
Not at all. Your father wanted
to send you to Krasnodar.


00:28:52.328 --> 00:28:55.118
- Say thanks, I was against it.
- That's typical of him.


00:28:55.278 --> 00:28:58.368
His panacea in every thorny
situation: Out of sight, out of mind!


00:28:58.528 --> 00:29:01.158
But it's not settled yet.
You might still go.


00:29:01.168 --> 00:29:03.788
Send me wherever
you want, I don't care.


00:29:04.398 --> 00:29:06.778
Yulia, what's your WiFi password?


00:29:06.948 --> 00:29:10.168
I want to post a photo I took of
the UFO, while it's still of interest.


00:29:10.238 --> 00:29:13.658
Should be nine, nine times,
but officially, I don't know.


00:29:13.818 --> 00:29:18.118
At the barracks, the commander only
gives the WiFi password for good behaviour.


00:29:18.278 --> 00:29:20.528
Excuse me, I have to go.


00:29:20.698 --> 00:29:24.528
Then go. Go fight your aliens.


00:29:24.698 --> 00:29:27.698
- You're better at that.
- Thank you for coming.


00:29:41.958 --> 00:29:43.958
SCHOOL 1191


00:29:45.278 --> 00:29:48.158
Hi Yulia! Check this out!


00:29:49.948 --> 00:29:52.818
- If you please!
- So, that's how it's going to be?


00:29:52.988 --> 00:29:54.278
Cool! Hi!


00:29:54.448 --> 00:29:56.027
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:29:56.867 --> 00:29:57.867
Hi.


00:30:04.867 --> 00:30:06.367
How are you?


00:30:09.407 --> 00:30:10.447
I'm fine.


00:30:41.947 --> 00:30:46.237
Guys. I perfectly understand
how hard it is for you.


00:30:47.077 --> 00:30:49.867
We all have lost loved ones, friends.


00:30:52.157 --> 00:30:56.157
But despite the bitterness of loss,
one cannot give in to anger.


00:30:57.027 --> 00:30:59.277
You cannot. People.


00:31:00.277 --> 00:31:06.027
For thousands of years, we've waited for a
encounter with an extraterrestrial civilisation.


00:31:06.197 --> 00:31:07.527
That's ended now!


00:31:07.697 --> 00:31:11.277
We have no idea what moral
standards the aliens have,


00:31:11.447 --> 00:31:14.397
what they think about life, death.
Do they understand the pain of a loss?


00:31:14.397 --> 00:31:16.857
If they don't, why should
I explain it to them?


00:31:16.987 --> 00:31:19.117
Why should we establish contact?


00:31:19.277 --> 00:31:21.237
Why can't we just get rid of them?


00:31:21.407 --> 00:31:23.447
Because this is a unique
chance for all mankind.


00:31:23.617 --> 00:31:27.067
A chance to die?! To give
your house to some freaks?


00:31:29.327 --> 00:31:32.486
A chance to learn
something about ourselves.


00:31:32.656 --> 00:31:37.366
To find out who we are.
Maybe even... to find a home.


00:31:37.526 --> 00:31:40.156
I know all about myself. I'm home!


00:31:40.326 --> 00:31:42.446
- And I didn't invite them in!
- Yulia, I...


00:31:42.616 --> 00:31:46.616
If not for them, everything would be
fine. And Sveta would be alive!


00:31:46.776 --> 00:31:47.986
Yulia...


00:32:14.156 --> 00:32:16.786
<i>In the service of the Motherland
Lebedev V. Yu.</i>


00:32:25.366 --> 00:32:27.736
Guys, check out this video
posted on VKontakte.


00:32:27.906 --> 00:32:28.906
Come here, Python!


00:32:37.326 --> 00:32:38.566
Go back to the start.


00:32:38.736 --> 00:32:40.486
Wait, there's more.


00:32:40.656 --> 00:32:41.906
Nits!


00:32:43.406 --> 00:32:45.216
Acting as if they were at home!


00:32:45.276 --> 00:32:48.446
Almost a billion views.
- Listen, the whole world saw it.


00:32:48.616 --> 00:32:51.836
Let's see how many views it will have
when these blood suckers spread.


00:32:51.906 --> 00:32:54.026
You think they'll break out of the cordon?


00:32:54.486 --> 00:32:57.696
What do you think they're here for?
To hang around your house?


00:32:57.866 --> 00:33:03.236
Well, I know, I... reposted all these videos.
Made some demotivators.


00:33:03.406 --> 00:33:06.236
We could start a trend on the Net.


00:33:07.276 --> 00:33:09.195
Very brave, guys! Well done!


00:33:10.115 --> 00:33:11.275
Yulia?


00:33:11.735 --> 00:33:14.025
All you can do is post, re-tweet and like.


00:33:14.195 --> 00:33:16.905
- Listen, friend. Watch your tongue,
- Sit down!


00:33:17.075 --> 00:33:19.655
Sit down? Tell this bimbo to sit down.


00:33:20.905 --> 00:33:22.985
She's not a bimbo, she's my girl.


00:33:23.155 --> 00:33:24.405
Oh yeah?


00:33:25.775 --> 00:33:27.365
She looks like a bimbo to me.


00:33:28.025 --> 00:33:29.115
Calm down!


00:33:29.275 --> 00:33:31.275
- Come here!
- Stop it!


00:33:32.655 --> 00:33:34.195
That's enough!


00:33:34.365 --> 00:33:35.365
Break it off!


00:33:35.525 --> 00:33:37.815
She's my girl, is that clear?!


00:33:37.985 --> 00:33:39.655
And I love her, you understand?


00:33:39.815 --> 00:33:42.565
Or do I have to say it again, huh?


00:33:43.775 --> 00:33:46.445
And I love you! Is that clear?


00:33:49.155 --> 00:33:50.565
Idiot!


00:33:55.615 --> 00:33:57.815
- What are you going to do?
- What do you suggest?


00:33:57.985 --> 00:34:00.695
Go there to prove who's
in charge in the district?


00:34:00.865 --> 00:34:03.945
- Yes!
- Opa, opa, opa!


00:34:04.155 --> 00:34:05.565
America, Europa!


00:34:05.735 --> 00:34:07.905
And what about the cordon?


00:34:08.075 --> 00:34:10.615
I mean, if the soldiers weren't
there, I would go myself.


00:34:10.775 --> 00:34:13.695
We can't just sit around and
wait. After what they did.


00:34:13.865 --> 00:34:15.615
We shouldn't, Tyoma.


00:34:16.115 --> 00:34:17.195
Of course.


00:34:18.615 --> 00:34:20.315
And we won't.


00:34:22.365 --> 00:34:25.405
There's a way in, the soldiers
don't even know about it.


00:34:26.735 --> 00:34:32.485
<i>A fortified fence has been
erected in this district.</i>


00:34:32.655 --> 00:34:35.865
<i>Unauthorized access to
the enclosed area...</i>


00:34:48.074 --> 00:34:51.194
Curfew in half an hour.
Let's go, boys!


00:35:01.114 --> 00:35:02.114
Hold this.


00:35:02.984 --> 00:35:04.984
The old processing plant.


00:35:05.524 --> 00:35:06.944
<i>It's been closed for 20 years.</i>


00:35:07.734 --> 00:35:09.694
My father used to work here.


00:35:09.864 --> 00:35:11.814
Finally, some good out of it.


00:35:25.114 --> 00:35:28.734
The plan: We go inside quietly
and carefully.


00:35:28.904 --> 00:35:31.064
If we meet our people,
we take them with us.


00:35:31.194 --> 00:35:34.114
If we find the aliens, we observe
them, but from a distance.


00:35:34.444 --> 00:35:37.114
We have to understand what they
want, and then tell everyone.


00:35:37.274 --> 00:35:39.024
Just don't play the hero.


00:35:39.194 --> 00:35:40.814
Rus, especially you.


00:35:40.984 --> 00:35:43.154
- You owe me another five.
- You'll get it back!


00:36:08.864 --> 00:36:09.864
Patrol's coming.


00:36:31.613 --> 00:36:34.533
Keep going. And you, stay here.
It's dangerous ahead.


00:36:34.533 --> 00:36:37.163
- I said I'm coming.
- Sit down! Sit down!


00:36:42.733 --> 00:36:45.493
If need be, shoot, and we'll come running.


00:37:06.813 --> 00:37:08.363
Seems to be empty.


00:37:25.653 --> 00:37:26.903
- Tyoma!
- Why are you yelling?!


00:37:27.073 --> 00:37:28.863
Tyoma, come here.


00:37:35.903 --> 00:37:37.193
<i>Is that, like, a bomb?</i>


00:37:42.273 --> 00:37:43.863
<i>Probably fell through the ceiling.</i>


00:38:45.072 --> 00:38:47.862
<i>Yul, damn it!
I understand, love and so on.</i>


00:38:47.862 --> 00:38:49.952
<i>But what's going on here is beautiful.</i>


00:38:49.982 --> 00:38:52.892
<i>Just unbelievable.
Come back quickly!</i>


00:39:31.572 --> 00:39:32.732
- Yulia!
- Up there!


00:39:54.071 --> 00:39:55.441
Higher! I know where!


00:39:55.611 --> 00:39:58.861
- Where are you going?
- I think it was here!


00:40:01.071 --> 00:40:02.271
Left!


00:40:02.731 --> 00:40:03.901
Yulia!


00:40:06.321 --> 00:40:07.561
Go downstairs!


00:40:10.691 --> 00:40:12.151
There he is!


00:40:12.691 --> 00:40:14.691
- Zhenya!
- Quiet! Don't yell!


00:40:23.981 --> 00:40:25.481
Yulia!


00:40:32.191 --> 00:40:34.231
So, let's go down!


00:40:39.441 --> 00:40:40.941
What's this?


00:40:45.901 --> 00:40:47.521
A kind of armour.


00:40:52.691 --> 00:40:53.691
Just like ours.


00:40:56.901 --> 00:40:58.611
Where's the creature?


00:41:08.731 --> 00:41:09.901
Rus...


00:41:10.980 --> 00:41:12.650
We're taking it.


00:41:30.770 --> 00:41:31.770
Quiet!


00:41:31.980 --> 00:41:34.060
- Patrol! Let's get away!
- What about this?


00:41:34.230 --> 00:41:36.610
- Leave it! Help us!
- It's heavy.


00:41:36.770 --> 00:41:38.400
Drop it, run!


00:41:38.570 --> 00:41:39.810
Help us!


00:41:39.980 --> 00:41:41.480
Come on, come on!


00:41:42.690 --> 00:41:43.690
Faster!


00:41:46.570 --> 00:41:50.280
<i>An object has been discovered,
probably of extraterrestrial origin.</i>


00:41:50.280 --> 00:41:52.660
<i>Don't touch anything!</i>


00:41:54.570 --> 00:41:55.940
Switch on the light!


00:41:57.940 --> 00:41:59.190
One two...


00:42:00.570 --> 00:42:01.860
Hook it!


00:42:04.270 --> 00:42:05.860
Fly, my dear.


00:42:13.110 --> 00:42:14.940
Well... What now?


00:42:16.860 --> 00:42:19.650
Should we give it to the military?


00:42:19.810 --> 00:42:22.310
We'll sort it out tomorrow.


00:42:22.940 --> 00:42:24.410
Now, off to bed.


00:43:41.939 --> 00:43:42.939
Hey!


00:44:54.108 --> 00:44:55.308
Hi!


00:44:58.608 --> 00:44:59.608
Okay, Google.


00:44:59.768 --> 00:45:01.768
- You want to study medicine, don't you?
- Yes.


00:45:01.938 --> 00:45:04.268
Can you skip the class?


00:45:04.438 --> 00:45:06.228
I really need you.


00:45:14.318 --> 00:45:15.608
Wow!


00:45:16.938 --> 00:45:19.518
That's just freaking awesome!


00:45:19.688 --> 00:45:21.688
The humanoid type, just like I told you all.


00:45:21.858 --> 00:45:25.728
They found water in our system, and
there's a trillion planets in the galaxy.


00:45:25.808 --> 00:45:28.038
The probability of life is 99.9.


00:45:28.108 --> 00:45:31.268
Everyone has been excited about
their alien suits, but the...


00:45:32.068 --> 00:45:33.858
Can you calm down?


00:45:34.018 --> 00:45:36.188
Think about what we can do.


00:45:36.938 --> 00:45:38.608
We need a doctor.


00:45:38.768 --> 00:45:39.978
Seriously?


00:45:40.148 --> 00:45:43.118
And I wouldn't have guessed
about it myself. No doctor!


00:45:43.118 --> 00:45:46.658
- The military would capture him! Get it?
- Well, so what?


00:45:48.188 --> 00:45:51.058
He saved my life, I owe him.


00:45:54.608 --> 00:45:55.608
Hold this.


00:46:03.187 --> 00:46:06.687
There seems to be
no visible fractures.


00:46:06.857 --> 00:46:08.017
He needs blood.


00:46:08.187 --> 00:46:09.707
- He's lost a lot.
- Our blood?


00:46:09.767 --> 00:46:14.147
Well, yes. He's breathing our air
and his anatomy is similar to ours.


00:46:14.317 --> 00:46:16.437
His blood might also be similar to ours.


00:46:16.607 --> 00:46:19.767
The truth is, there's a
chance it could kill him.


00:46:19.937 --> 00:46:22.587
But without a transfusion,
he'll definitely die.


00:46:26.187 --> 00:46:28.437
You're calling an ambulance, right?


00:46:28.607 --> 00:46:30.937
Dad's friend is a doctor.


00:46:31.107 --> 00:46:33.227
He treated me after they crashed.


00:46:33.397 --> 00:46:36.057
Igor Semyonovich?
Hi, this is Yulia.


00:46:36.477 --> 00:46:39.727
You said to call you if
the headache came back.


00:46:41.017 --> 00:46:42.577
Yes, can I come right now?


00:46:42.647 --> 00:46:45.057
And please ask for a transit
permit for the car.


00:46:45.227 --> 00:46:46.227
Thank you.


00:46:48.767 --> 00:46:51.407
You take a picture of him,
I'll kill you, understand?


00:46:52.067 --> 00:46:53.677
Hey, wait! Where are you going?


00:46:54.717 --> 00:46:58.857
Haematology. Igor Semyonovich's orders.
This is urgent. A VIP. No registration.


00:46:58.937 --> 00:47:00.307
This way!


00:47:00.477 --> 00:47:01.307
Attention!


00:47:02.567 --> 00:47:03.937
Here it is!


00:47:05.517 --> 00:47:06.517
Stop!


00:47:09.647 --> 00:47:11.187
And if we're discovered?


00:47:11.357 --> 00:47:14.767
Then I'll say, it was your plan and
you forcibly dragged me here.


00:47:14.937 --> 00:47:17.387
Will you stay for me? I'll kiss you.


00:47:19.187 --> 00:47:22.327
Wait... Isn't it how you
get someone to betray their country?


00:47:22.397 --> 00:47:24.107
Absolutely! Come on now!


00:47:24.267 --> 00:47:25.647
- On three.
- What?


00:47:25.807 --> 00:47:26.807
Three!


00:47:28.477 --> 00:47:30.837
- Close the door, turn the light off!
- Yes!


00:48:02.396 --> 00:48:04.556
- Finger!
- Which one?


00:48:04.726 --> 00:48:05.856
The middle.


00:48:07.316 --> 00:48:09.056
One, two, three.


00:48:11.356 --> 00:48:13.976
Well, theoretically, it should work.


00:48:14.266 --> 00:48:17.146
There you are!
His blood group is A positive.


00:48:17.316 --> 00:48:20.456
Well, according to our classification.
But considering it's from the humanoid...


00:48:20.516 --> 00:48:22.156
Enough! I'm A+ too!


00:48:22.226 --> 00:48:24.976
Lie down. No, sit down, sit down.


00:48:25.146 --> 00:48:26.306
So...


00:48:27.896 --> 00:48:30.436
So, insert the needle parallel to the vein,


00:48:30.606 --> 00:48:33.106
then find the vein, at the
angle of 45 degrees...


00:48:33.266 --> 00:48:35.396
- Come on!
- Just a second.


00:48:35.566 --> 00:48:37.396
OK. One, two, three!


00:48:37.566 --> 00:48:39.146
No, stop!


00:48:41.356 --> 00:48:42.976
Are you kidding me?


00:48:48.766 --> 00:48:49.976
Oh, come on!


00:50:51.474 --> 00:50:52.474
Yulia.


00:50:52.804 --> 00:50:55.394
Just go. You need to sleep.


00:50:55.394 --> 00:50:58.014
Don't worry. I'll stay with him.
Everything will be fine.


00:50:58.064 --> 00:51:02.014
But no photos or posts like "I'm
treating an alien". You hear?


00:51:02.184 --> 00:51:05.694
- I'll be silent like a tomb!
- A tomb without WiFi and 4G.


00:52:46.563 --> 00:52:49.933
No heat emission, no radioactivity,
no thermal reading.


00:52:51.763 --> 00:52:53.473
Absolute symmetry.


00:52:54.143 --> 00:52:57.103
Some kind of a spherical
horse in a vacuum.


00:52:59.643 --> 00:53:00.643
A weapon?


00:53:02.013 --> 00:53:04.353
- I don't know yet.
- Well then.


00:53:33.353 --> 00:53:37.183
Judging by the movement of
water masses and air fronts,


00:53:37.353 --> 00:53:40.013
the ship draws water like a magnet.


00:53:40.183 --> 00:53:42.753
Are the going to take over
by depriving us of water, or what?


00:53:42.753 --> 00:53:46.923
In our opinion, they need the water
for the regeneration of the ship.


00:53:47.063 --> 00:53:50.803
About 30% of the external
damage caused by the crash


00:53:50.973 --> 00:53:52.143
has been repaired.


00:53:52.313 --> 00:53:56.093
We've obtained a piece of their technology,
and it shows the same properties,


00:53:56.093 --> 00:53:58.253
but its function remains unknown.


00:53:59.013 --> 00:54:01.223
- A weapon?
- Or an element of the ship.


00:54:01.393 --> 00:54:03.252
People are already gathering
at the checkpoint.


00:54:03.262 --> 00:54:07.252
Rumours are spreading on the Net
that we're hiding the scale of water loss.


00:54:07.392 --> 00:54:09.672
As if the boat hadn't
already started to rock.


00:54:09.672 --> 00:54:13.122
Well, take a decision! Connect
the town hall to the television


00:54:13.122 --> 00:54:16.402
- and let them report every hour.
- We've already taken steps.


00:54:16.402 --> 00:54:20.002
Water trucks at the checkpoint.
Water distribution inside the perimeter.


00:54:20.002 --> 00:54:25.092
And what do you think we should
do about this element of the ship?


00:54:26.892 --> 00:54:29.612
- I suggest we return it.
- To whom? Them?!


00:54:29.682 --> 00:54:31.722
We don't know their intentions.


00:54:31.892 --> 00:54:35.702
Our main task is to minimize the
possibility of open conflict.


00:54:35.762 --> 00:54:37.272
Lebedev!


00:54:37.272 --> 00:54:40.342
You were recommended as a
good commander for the rearguard,


00:54:40.342 --> 00:54:42.712
not as an expert on
extraterrestrial cultures.


00:54:42.852 --> 00:54:44.852
- Allow me to go?
- Where?


00:54:44.852 --> 00:54:48.032
- To the rear.
- Please, don't take offence, Colonel!


00:54:48.102 --> 00:54:50.552
We're not here on a first date!


00:54:51.802 --> 00:54:53.102
Well then.


00:54:54.562 --> 00:54:57.302
Your suggestion is good, but
we won't give anything back.


00:54:57.302 --> 00:55:00.562
They may know all about us, but we
don't know anything about them.


00:55:00.602 --> 00:55:02.682
And that very element...


00:55:03.892 --> 00:55:05.762
is the only thing we have.


00:55:19.222 --> 00:55:21.222
What are you sitting here for?


00:55:21.392 --> 00:55:23.392
- He's there, well...
- What?


00:55:23.932 --> 00:55:24.972
He woke up.


00:55:33.262 --> 00:55:36.932
Crap, how can we communicate with him?


00:55:37.102 --> 00:55:40.221
In theory, there is some
universal sign language.


00:55:42.101 --> 00:55:43.511
Fuck!


00:55:44.761 --> 00:55:46.181
Don't be afraid.


00:55:48.561 --> 00:55:49.721
That's so cool!


00:55:49.891 --> 00:55:52.141
This is speech reconstruction!


00:55:52.311 --> 00:55:55.111
A few phrases, and he picked up
the structure of the language!


00:55:55.181 --> 00:55:58.301
A superior race, I told you!


00:55:58.471 --> 00:56:00.101
I'm Hakon.


00:56:02.471 --> 00:56:03.471
Pleased to meet you.


00:56:05.221 --> 00:56:06.221
You're not pleased.


00:56:06.391 --> 00:56:10.801
This is a complementary expression,
used as a rule on first acquaintance.


00:56:10.971 --> 00:56:13.681
I'm Google by the way,
if you're interested.


00:56:14.511 --> 00:56:15.511
Is it yours?


00:56:15.511 --> 00:56:16.511
- Yes.
- Take it off!


00:56:16.511 --> 00:56:20.311
- Too late, conjugation's already done.
- The transfer of genetic material.


00:56:20.311 --> 00:56:23.041
- It means you're stuck with it!
- I understood!


00:56:23.041 --> 00:56:26.911
- Why are you here? What do you want?
- I think they want to civilize us.


00:56:26.911 --> 00:56:29.531
They're bringing new
technologies to help humanity.


00:56:29.531 --> 00:56:31.191
Am I right?


00:56:32.311 --> 00:56:34.851
No? Then...


00:56:35.311 --> 00:56:37.891
All you want is to extinguish
all life, or what?


00:56:38.061 --> 00:56:39.261
This is a difficult question.


00:56:39.431 --> 00:56:41.101
Don't move!


00:56:41.261 --> 00:56:44.011
I need to go back. To find Shilk.


00:56:48.471 --> 00:56:49.471
Get dressed!


00:56:58.801 --> 00:57:01.351
Has he already learned
the word for thanks, huh?


00:57:01.511 --> 00:57:03.971
Thank you is a form of gratitude.


00:57:04.141 --> 00:57:09.011
She... is kinda grateful
to you... for saving her.


00:57:10.351 --> 00:57:13.051
You think you saved the
enemy, and you feel awful,


00:57:13.111 --> 00:57:15.460
and if I said thank you,
you'd feel better.


00:57:46.470 --> 00:57:47.930
Are you ready?


00:57:48.560 --> 00:57:50.800
- Then bugger off now!
- What does that mean?


00:57:50.970 --> 00:57:52.470
Fuck off! Clear off!


00:57:52.640 --> 00:57:55.850
Get the hell out of my garage
and off this planet, understood?


00:58:07.640 --> 00:58:08.640
Get out!


00:58:34.560 --> 00:58:36.220
Why are you looking at me?


00:58:36.390 --> 00:58:39.470
He's the superior race, kinda.
He'll find his people.


00:58:39.640 --> 00:58:41.760
Theoretically, yes. But imagining...


00:58:41.930 --> 00:58:44.430
Stop being a smart ass.


00:59:03.889 --> 00:59:05.099
Excuse me!


00:59:05.259 --> 00:59:06.889
I'm talking to you!


00:59:08.099 --> 00:59:09.759
Please stop!


00:59:15.559 --> 00:59:17.299
Where are you going?


00:59:18.139 --> 00:59:19.469
I'm just going.


00:59:19.639 --> 00:59:21.929
First, your papers, then you
can go wherever you want.


00:59:21.999 --> 00:59:25.119
What's going on with this buffoon?
Let's pick him up.


00:59:26.259 --> 00:59:27.259
The arms!


00:59:30.849 --> 00:59:32.139
Another one!


00:59:35.849 --> 00:59:37.779
Here you go.
I'll pick it up later.


00:59:37.799 --> 00:59:38.799
Hide it!


00:59:41.389 --> 00:59:42.389
Stop!


00:59:42.889 --> 00:59:43.889
Stop!


00:59:54.429 --> 00:59:55.429
Crap!


00:59:55.889 --> 00:59:58.469
This doesn't make sense.
You can't cut it.


01:00:10.509 --> 01:00:11.849
Fuck me!


01:00:15.559 --> 01:00:18.479
Think about how much dough
you'd get for this thing


01:00:18.479 --> 01:00:19.819
in an online auction.


01:00:23.429 --> 01:00:25.679
Guys, check this out.


01:00:27.509 --> 01:00:30.048
It doesn't weight anything
when you wear it.


01:00:30.968 --> 01:00:32.548
I'm an Avatar, get it?


01:00:33.058 --> 01:00:36.008
It's a kind of an exoskeleton.


01:00:38.178 --> 01:00:40.388
And it's the right size for a human.


01:00:43.098 --> 01:00:44.598
Guys!


01:00:45.428 --> 01:00:47.388
Take this shit off me!


01:00:47.558 --> 01:00:49.798
Pull out your hand!


01:00:49.968 --> 01:00:51.258
Stretch your arm!


01:00:51.428 --> 01:00:53.178
Pull!


01:00:55.638 --> 01:00:57.218
Call an ambulance!


01:00:57.388 --> 01:00:59.608
Are they just cuts?
What are you yelling?


01:00:59.678 --> 01:01:02.718
Fuck your aliens! Why are
you still wanting to resist.


01:01:02.888 --> 01:01:06.418
They're a hundred times stronger than you!
You'll soon see, all of you.


01:01:06.418 --> 01:01:08.198
- Fuck off!
- What you talking about?


01:01:08.208 --> 01:01:10.748
- Take your things and scram!
- Don't touch me!


01:01:11.508 --> 01:01:14.758
- Come on, go home!
- Leave me alone!


01:01:15.308 --> 01:01:16.798
- It's enough, Rus!
- What's enough?


01:01:16.968 --> 01:01:18.748
- Chill out!
- Think you're so smart?


01:01:18.748 --> 01:01:21.628
You'll be the first. The first
to die! Do you understand?


01:01:21.758 --> 01:01:23.798
- Go home!
- Chill out!


01:01:25.218 --> 01:01:27.298
What the fuck are we going
to do with it?


01:01:34.678 --> 01:01:35.928
We'll give it up.


01:01:36.798 --> 01:01:38.008
To whom?


01:01:39.558 --> 01:01:42.008
- I'll call on Yulia's father to decide.
- Seriously?!


01:01:42.178 --> 01:01:44.638
- What do you suggest?
- Sell it?


01:01:48.348 --> 01:01:50.468
- Why not?
- I'll call him.


01:01:58.058 --> 01:02:00.718
Hello, Valentin Yuryevich?
This is Artyom.


01:02:00.888 --> 01:02:02.678
No, she's not with me.


01:02:02.848 --> 01:02:06.177
- I have to show you something.
- Don't be like that with him.


01:02:06.347 --> 01:02:08.597
- Could you come by?
- Why not?


01:02:08.757 --> 01:02:12.387
Then I'll come to you. It's
quite urgent. I'm serious.


01:02:14.637 --> 01:02:15.927
Yes, I understand.


01:02:18.797 --> 01:02:19.797
Thank you.


01:02:20.887 --> 01:02:25.007
Citizens, water is limited
to 5 litres per person.


01:02:25.177 --> 01:02:28.047
Why so little?
I have children at home!


01:02:28.597 --> 01:02:32.887
Free hotel rooms with all amenities
are available for those who wish.


01:02:33.057 --> 01:02:34.597
Go get one yourself!


01:02:34.757 --> 01:02:36.347
People are angry.


01:02:37.387 --> 01:02:39.307
At least they're distributing water.


01:02:40.097 --> 01:02:42.047
I repeat!


01:02:42.217 --> 01:02:47.797
Free hotel rooms with all amenities
are available for those who wish.


01:02:51.557 --> 01:02:53.387
Greetings, comrade Major.


01:02:54.797 --> 01:02:57.297
Is Colonel Lebedev here?


01:02:57.467 --> 01:02:59.507
- Valentin Yuryevich?
- Hasn't arrived yet.


01:03:01.347 --> 01:03:04.847
What's going on here? Did you
retrieve something out there?


01:03:05.177 --> 01:03:06.637
- Move the car away!
- Why?


01:03:06.797 --> 01:03:09.847
- This is a safety zone. Move the car!
- We'll leave right away, quietly.


01:03:10.007 --> 01:03:12.257
- Move the car away now!
- I'm not going anywhere.


01:03:12.427 --> 01:03:14.387
Why so rough? This is our neighbourhood!


01:03:14.557 --> 01:03:17.757
- Leave it! Stop it!
- I didn't touch him.


01:03:17.927 --> 01:03:19.927
We'll leave right away.


01:03:33.097 --> 01:03:34.257
Don't hit him!


01:03:34.967 --> 01:03:36.217
What are you doing?!


01:03:46.306 --> 01:03:49.296
Tosha! Anton! Get up, buddy!


01:03:49.466 --> 01:03:50.966
Come on, help me!


01:03:51.136 --> 01:03:52.716
Take him away!


01:03:53.556 --> 01:03:55.006
Disperse!


01:03:56.136 --> 01:03:57.926
Citizens! Disperse!


01:03:57.926 --> 01:04:00.416
- Tyom, get in the car!
- I said, take him away!


01:04:00.556 --> 01:04:02.256
Disperse immediately!


01:04:02.426 --> 01:04:04.716
Citizens, vacate these grounds!


01:04:04.886 --> 01:04:06.136
See you in the garage!


01:04:06.846 --> 01:04:11.346
In small groups. Don't panic.
Move in the direction of the subway!


01:04:11.676 --> 01:04:17.176
If you do not comply with
this order, force will be applied.


01:04:17.196 --> 01:04:21.196
<i>Move in the direction of the subway!</i>


01:04:22.216 --> 01:04:24.006
What are you doing?
Why are you doing this?


01:04:24.176 --> 01:04:25.596
Don't touch them!


01:04:26.056 --> 01:04:28.136
Where are you going,
old man? Go home!


01:04:29.556 --> 01:04:31.046
Stop!


01:04:33.926 --> 01:04:35.636
We're all the same people!


01:04:35.796 --> 01:04:39.396
It's enough! He has orders!
You want to be arrested?


01:04:41.426 --> 01:04:43.966
Are you still alive?
Come on, get up.


01:04:50.636 --> 01:04:51.756
Corridor formation!


01:04:51.926 --> 01:04:55.796
- Don't struggle, it'll just be more painful.
- Close the ranks!


01:05:12.716 --> 01:05:14.546
Hurry!


01:05:14.716 --> 01:05:17.096
Greetings, Valentin Yuryevich!


01:05:19.965 --> 01:05:21.295
Wait a moment.


01:05:22.215 --> 01:05:24.095
Well, what did you want to say?


01:05:24.255 --> 01:05:25.635
Wait!


01:05:35.675 --> 01:05:39.095
I was just missing you.
We're not strangers.


01:05:39.255 --> 01:05:42.585
We could sit down like a family,
talk, have a cup of tea, huh?


01:05:42.585 --> 01:05:46.245
I don't understand. Is it too
early for you to talk or too late?


01:05:46.385 --> 01:05:47.715
Too late!


01:05:48.595 --> 01:05:51.675
Yulia was right, you don't
understand shit!


01:05:53.175 --> 01:05:56.385
You're the king of Moscow,
aren't you? You've got everything.


01:05:56.555 --> 01:06:00.145
Soldiers, cars, planes circling
around. You built a pretty fence.


01:06:00.145 --> 01:06:01.725
You even have horses!


01:06:01.755 --> 01:06:03.675
Stay away from Yulia!


01:06:18.885 --> 01:06:20.045
Take him away.


01:06:27.925 --> 01:06:30.345
Don't stand like this.
Give me your hand.


01:06:32.555 --> 01:06:36.845
- Junkie. Picked up on the street.
- God, the circus with horses!


01:06:37.755 --> 01:06:41.785
<i>... a fragment, presumably from the
so-called flying saucer, was retrieved.</i>


01:06:41.885 --> 01:06:44.475
Where do you think you're
going? Don't move.


01:06:45.795 --> 01:06:49.095
<i>This mysterious object is now
with the Ministry of Defence,</i>


01:06:49.255 --> 01:06:52.635
<i>where its experts
continue to investigate...</i>


01:06:54.844 --> 01:06:56.674
Did you cut the tips off?


01:07:00.054 --> 01:07:03.704
Vasya, this asshole doesn't have
fingertips. What should I do with him?


01:07:03.704 --> 01:07:05.084
Register him as unknown.


01:07:05.174 --> 01:07:07.134
Let the military take care of him.


01:07:25.794 --> 01:07:29.164
Good day, comrade Colonel.
A friend of mine is detained here.


01:07:29.164 --> 01:07:32.744
That tall, funny hat, old coat.
Have you seen him?


01:07:33.214 --> 01:07:36.214
I am Lebedeva, Yulia.
Valentin Yuryevich's daughter.


01:07:37.304 --> 01:07:40.504
- Do I need to know that?
- Actually, yes.


01:07:40.674 --> 01:07:44.634
In case of declaration of martial law, the
military assumes governmental authority.


01:07:44.794 --> 01:07:49.754
<i>The commander in charge of the perimeter,
Valentin Lebedev, refrained from commenting.</i>


01:07:50.304 --> 01:07:51.594
All right.


01:07:54.344 --> 01:07:55.634
Yulia Valentinovna.


01:07:56.304 --> 01:07:59.254
Yes, your friend is quite
peculiar, Yulia Valentinovna.


01:08:00.794 --> 01:08:03.184
It's just that he's from St. Petersburg.


01:08:04.714 --> 01:08:05.714
Yulia?


01:08:06.594 --> 01:08:07.644
- Yul!
- Let's go!


01:08:07.664 --> 01:08:08.704
Yul!


01:08:09.004 --> 01:08:10.294
- Yul!
- Wait for me!


01:08:10.464 --> 01:08:11.594
- Yul!
- Stop!


01:08:11.754 --> 01:08:14.754
- What happened to your face?
- It's alright, Princess!


01:08:15.214 --> 01:08:17.334
When it's healed, I'll be
even more beautiful!


01:08:17.334 --> 01:08:19.614
I'll call my father, he'll
get you out of here!


01:08:19.614 --> 01:08:22.614
To hell with him!
I don't need any help from him!


01:08:22.714 --> 01:08:24.424
Can you hear me?
It's very important.


01:08:24.594 --> 01:08:27.384
- I have to talk to you!
- Just go. We'll figure it out.


01:08:27.554 --> 01:08:29.204
I just want to talk!
Let me through!


01:08:29.204 --> 01:08:32.083
Tell your commander,
everything's about to change!


01:08:32.213 --> 01:08:34.673
The whole area will soon be ours!


01:08:34.843 --> 01:08:36.593
That'll be crazy!


01:08:40.003 --> 01:08:43.673
You have to react when they talk to you!
Then there are fewer questions.


01:08:43.843 --> 01:08:46.413
If you don't know what
to say, at least smile!


01:08:46.413 --> 01:08:48.063
It would really help.


01:08:57.423 --> 01:08:58.523
Something like that.


01:09:03.673 --> 01:09:05.493
Come, I'll take you
to the perimeter.


01:09:05.503 --> 01:09:08.743
Shilk is no longer there. Armed
men took it away. I saw it.


01:09:08.883 --> 01:09:11.543
And without that Shilk, you
can't get on the ship?


01:09:11.543 --> 01:09:13.063
Home is 47 light years away.


01:09:13.063 --> 01:09:15.293
A transition is necessary
to contract time.


01:09:15.293 --> 01:09:17.793
And without Shilk, flesh cannot
withstand the transition.


01:09:18.133 --> 01:09:21.263
So you get your Shilk, and
leave immediately, right?


01:09:21.383 --> 01:09:22.963
Do you want to help?


01:09:25.053 --> 01:09:27.293
I can help.
There's a difference.


01:09:28.753 --> 01:09:29.963
Take that off!


01:09:30.963 --> 01:09:33.003
You'll melt! Come along.


01:09:33.173 --> 01:09:35.173
<i>I don't know if our
camera can show this,</i>


01:09:35.343 --> 01:09:37.793
<i>but to the naked eye,
a change of colour is apparent.</i>


01:09:37.963 --> 01:09:41.543
<i>Half an hour ago, we noticed that
the object was acquiring a reddish tint.</i>


01:09:41.713 --> 01:09:46.173
<i>So far, we've not received any comment
from the unified information centre,</i>


01:09:46.343 --> 01:09:50.543
<i>however, I doubt that anyone could say
anything definitive about the phenomenon.</i>


01:09:51.133 --> 01:09:53.293
Hey, guys, come over here!


01:09:54.343 --> 01:09:56.713
- Why are you here?
- I am Yulia Lebedeva, the daughter.


01:09:56.883 --> 01:09:59.223
Please tell my father
I need to talk to him.


01:09:59.223 --> 01:10:01.053
He doesn't answer his phone.


01:10:06.203 --> 01:10:07.202
Lebedev's daughter...


01:10:07.202 --> 01:10:10.162
First we need a pass. Without
one, we won't get anywhere.


01:10:10.502 --> 01:10:12.752
Then we'll find out
where exactly it is.


01:10:14.252 --> 01:10:17.212
He's in a meeting. He'll call
you as soon as he's free.


01:10:23.752 --> 01:10:26.382
Please, tell him that I'm pregnant.


01:10:31.552 --> 01:10:32.792
In which month?


01:10:34.002 --> 01:10:35.002
The third.


01:10:38.792 --> 01:10:41.212
Comrade officers, please
vacate the premises.


01:10:41.382 --> 01:10:43.092
Everyone leaves the room!


01:10:47.842 --> 01:10:50.172
- Who is this?
- One of the possible candidates.


01:10:51.302 --> 01:10:54.212
- What does that mean?
- Paternity is still unclear.


01:10:54.382 --> 01:10:57.462
We have to have DNA
testing, don't we, Kharitosha?


01:10:57.922 --> 01:10:58.962
Still unclear.


01:10:59.132 --> 01:11:03.502
Still unclear. But it's clear to me.
Did you serve in the army, Kharitosha?


01:11:03.882 --> 01:11:05.002
I didn't serve.


01:11:05.172 --> 01:11:08.592
So from tomorrow, you'll be at
the border guarding the homeland.


01:11:08.752 --> 01:11:10.172
In a submarine.


01:11:10.342 --> 01:11:12.952
And your Che Guevara will be
sent to the reformatory.


01:11:12.952 --> 01:11:14.912
Great! The baby will be an orphan.


01:11:15.052 --> 01:11:18.672
- I'll raise him.
- And if that doesn't work out?


01:11:27.212 --> 01:11:28.542
Dad.


01:11:30.132 --> 01:11:31.382
Hey Dad!


01:11:32.752 --> 01:11:35.042
Please, don't be angry. I beg you.


01:11:35.212 --> 01:11:39.712
It upsets me. And in my condition,
I shouldn't get upset, you know.


01:11:40.962 --> 01:11:43.881
I don't understand what's going on.


01:11:44.051 --> 01:11:45.591
You're angry.


01:11:45.751 --> 01:11:47.131
There's no need.


01:11:49.211 --> 01:11:50.631
Get out of here!


01:11:51.631 --> 01:11:52.631
I'm getting out.


01:11:52.791 --> 01:11:54.711
Come on, Haritosha, go!


01:11:57.051 --> 01:11:58.631
Is he wearing my clothes?!


01:11:58.791 --> 01:12:01.631
You worry about that?
You're not strangers anymore.


01:12:03.251 --> 01:12:06.041
So, why didn't you tell me sooner?


01:12:10.001 --> 01:12:12.211
You really believed that, didn't you?


01:12:28.251 --> 01:12:32.091
So you think it's funny, right?
Is this supposed to be a joke?


01:12:32.591 --> 01:12:35.341
Do you think I have time
to listen to this moron?


01:12:35.501 --> 01:12:37.691
When's the last time you
listened to me so closely?


01:12:37.751 --> 01:12:40.331
Took interest in what's
going on in my life? Tell me.


01:12:57.381 --> 01:12:58.791
Valentin Yuryevich!


01:12:59.381 --> 01:13:02.591
A flying saucer crashed in our
city, if you didn't notice!


01:13:02.751 --> 01:13:05.941
But you don't care. You have
your dad here to fix everything!


01:13:06.131 --> 01:13:09.441
And when the aliens have left,
what new excuse will you think of?


01:13:15.421 --> 01:13:16.591
How?


01:13:21.340 --> 01:13:22.340
That wasn't Lebedev!


01:13:22.340 --> 01:13:24.750
That wasn't Lebedev!
Raise the alarm!


01:13:27.000 --> 01:13:30.540
<i>Warning! All personnel must take...</i>


01:13:30.540 --> 01:13:33.040
Why am I surprised? You
never gave a damn about me.


01:13:33.170 --> 01:13:35.890
Even when mom was dying, you
didn't let me say goodbye.


01:13:35.890 --> 01:13:37.760
You said she was getting better.


01:13:37.790 --> 01:13:41.630
I just didn't want it to
happen... before your eyes.


01:13:41.790 --> 01:13:44.420
But you didn't even think of
asking me what I wanted?


01:13:44.490 --> 01:13:47.610
Maybe I wanted to spend the last
months of her life beside her,


01:13:47.610 --> 01:13:49.610
beside the only person
who understood me,


01:13:49.610 --> 01:13:51.630
and not at the summer camp disco.


01:13:51.630 --> 01:13:53.540
I'll never forgive you!


01:13:59.460 --> 01:14:03.000
First unit, block this road!
Don't retract the posts!


01:14:03.000 --> 01:14:05.110
- Deploy the spike strip!
- Yes, sir!


01:14:05.110 --> 01:14:07.890
Second unit, block the
main entrance! Quickly!


01:14:07.890 --> 01:14:09.730
No one must leave!


01:14:15.840 --> 01:14:17.540
- Andrei!
- Yes?


01:14:17.710 --> 01:14:19.380
- Yulia, home!
- Yes!


01:14:19.550 --> 01:14:22.090
- And this one here, to Kamchatka!
- Yes, Colonel!


01:14:23.050 --> 01:14:24.250
Get in!


01:14:25.750 --> 01:14:27.750
- Serving the galaxy!
- Very funny.


01:14:30.170 --> 01:14:33.000
Retract the posts! Let the car out!


01:14:53.550 --> 01:14:54.960
- Did Yulia call?
- No.


01:14:55.130 --> 01:14:56.209
Hi there!


01:14:56.379 --> 01:14:57.919
- How are you?
- OK


01:14:58.089 --> 01:15:00.879
- And you, superman?
- Everything's fine.


01:15:02.669 --> 01:15:06.259
- So, how do we get rid of the armour?
- Forget it, we keep it.


01:15:07.669 --> 01:15:09.499
Then what do we do, Tyoma?


01:15:10.419 --> 01:15:11.949
Defend the homeland!


01:15:11.949 --> 01:15:13.409
That's right!


01:15:38.209 --> 01:15:41.449
- We should have added aluminium shavings.
- Nah, it's enough as it is.


01:15:41.449 --> 01:15:43.199
Petrol and oil. Classic!


01:15:43.959 --> 01:15:45.669
Che Guevara did it like that.


01:16:03.419 --> 01:16:05.889
Hello, Tyoma, how are you?
Did they let you go?


01:16:05.889 --> 01:16:07.929
Of course! General amnesty!


01:16:09.379 --> 01:16:13.379
Listen, Yulia. I'm sorry for before...
At the police station, I wasn't myself.


01:16:14.129 --> 01:16:15.589
You wanted to talk to me.


01:16:15.749 --> 01:16:18.689
- Yes, but I can't right now...
- Want me to pick you up?


01:16:18.689 --> 01:16:20.479
We've started a movement, here.


01:16:20.789 --> 01:16:23.589
- You'll like it.
- Tyoma, I can't right now.


01:16:23.669 --> 01:16:25.669
Ah, I understand. Dad.


01:16:25.999 --> 01:16:26.999
It's OK


01:16:27.549 --> 01:16:30.039
Well, if you want to see me, come over.


01:16:30.209 --> 01:16:31.339
Yulia...


01:16:32.668 --> 01:16:33.788
I love you.


01:16:36.498 --> 01:16:37.628
Bye, Tyoma.


01:16:50.748 --> 01:16:53.738
I need the Shilk to get back on
the ship as soon as possible.


01:16:53.738 --> 01:16:57.078
Slow down! We're not going
in the restricted area now.


01:16:57.208 --> 01:16:59.878
Tell the guard the name of your father.


01:17:00.048 --> 01:17:01.208
Are you serious?


01:17:01.378 --> 01:17:04.378
Just a week in Moscow and your
plans already involve corruption?


01:17:04.388 --> 01:17:06.678
Until night comes,
we don't stand a chance!


01:17:06.708 --> 01:17:08.498
What do we do until then?


01:17:12.788 --> 01:17:14.628
You're as thin as a bean!


01:17:14.788 --> 01:17:16.418
Do you need something to eat?


01:17:16.588 --> 01:17:19.748
Or do you feed like...
with photosynthesis?


01:17:22.128 --> 01:17:23.248
Come along.


01:17:51.128 --> 01:17:53.088
Here we are, anyway.


01:17:58.548 --> 01:18:00.838
Charl! Hello!


01:18:01.878 --> 01:18:03.088
This is Charl.


01:18:08.548 --> 01:18:10.627
This creature is suffering, it's in pain.


01:18:10.787 --> 01:18:12.887
Yes, I know. She's very old.


01:18:12.957 --> 01:18:14.957
Dad says she should
be put to sleep.


01:18:15.127 --> 01:18:16.247
Put to sleep?


01:18:17.627 --> 01:18:18.787
Killed.


01:18:19.007 --> 01:18:20.287
But I can't.


01:18:20.587 --> 01:18:22.087
Charl's a family member.


01:18:22.247 --> 01:18:25.957
We bought her with my
mom. She's dead now.


01:18:26.127 --> 01:18:29.627
You like to think about your mom
so you let the creature suffer?


01:18:29.627 --> 01:18:30.917
No, on the contrary.


01:18:32.787 --> 01:18:34.537
Well, I need her.


01:18:34.707 --> 01:18:36.207
What for?


01:18:36.377 --> 01:18:38.377
You don't have feelings, do you?


01:18:38.547 --> 01:18:41.997
- We see and feel just like you.
- I don't mean that.


01:18:45.047 --> 01:18:46.787
Gratitude.


01:18:48.497 --> 01:18:49.997
Loneliness.


01:18:51.337 --> 01:18:52.667
Hatred.


01:18:56.087 --> 01:18:57.337
Love.


01:18:58.207 --> 01:19:00.937
Love and hate are needed
to overcome the fear of death.


01:19:00.937 --> 01:19:04.487
When there's no death, you
don't need love or hate.


01:19:05.377 --> 01:19:08.167
This is crazy. I'll put that
on my status, OK?


01:19:08.337 --> 01:19:11.607
Yulechka, don't you want to
introduce me to this young man?


01:19:13.417 --> 01:19:15.747
Of course. Hak... Khariton,


01:19:15.917 --> 01:19:17.377
this is Lyuba!


01:19:17.547 --> 01:19:18.917
Lyuba, this is Khariton.


01:19:19.087 --> 01:19:20.627
What an ancient name.


01:19:20.787 --> 01:19:23.337
Old enough to be put to sleep?


01:19:23.497 --> 01:19:25.167
- I'm sorry, what?
- Come along.


01:19:27.207 --> 01:19:30.587
Lyuba, he's from St.
Petersburg, you know?


01:19:31.247 --> 01:19:34.537
And once it was the cultural capital!


01:19:34.707 --> 01:19:35.707
Yes.


01:19:48.166 --> 01:19:50.206
What did you do with her?


01:19:50.376 --> 01:19:51.376
This is Shilk!


01:19:51.586 --> 01:19:53.996
When it's near, you can live forever.


01:19:54.586 --> 01:19:56.836
Charl! Charl! Come here.


01:19:59.996 --> 01:20:01.286
Healthy eyes!


01:20:01.456 --> 01:20:02.786
Healthy dog?


01:20:04.176 --> 01:20:05.256
Wait,


01:20:05.626 --> 01:20:08.136
are you... immortal?


01:20:09.586 --> 01:20:13.586
<i>Mikhail Igorevich, please tell
us about the first contact.</i>


01:20:14.206 --> 01:20:15.536
<i>A tragedy.</i>


01:20:15.706 --> 01:20:17.956
<i>A tragedy on a global scale.</i>


01:20:19.166 --> 01:20:23.916
<i>We were hoping to meet
reasonable, intelligent beings,</i>


01:20:24.086 --> 01:20:27.916
<i>with whom we could conduct a
dialogue and exchange technologies.</i>


01:20:28.086 --> 01:20:30.496
<i>But we're facing ugly creatures</i>


01:20:30.666 --> 01:20:33.786
<i>that attacked us at the
first opportunity.</i>


01:20:33.956 --> 01:20:35.626
- Don't be tempted.
- What's this?


01:20:35.786 --> 01:20:37.286
A dangerous thing.


01:20:37.456 --> 01:20:40.956
30 minutes of watching will
make an alien like you melt.


01:21:09.086 --> 01:21:10.456
It's delicious, thanks!


01:21:11.046 --> 01:21:12.246
You're welcome.


01:21:17.666 --> 01:21:19.246
MUSTARD


01:22:08.045 --> 01:22:09.995
What for?


01:22:10.165 --> 01:22:11.705
A joke.


01:22:21.495 --> 01:22:24.085
But that isn't funny.


01:22:25.995 --> 01:22:27.045
Eat, eat.


01:22:27.065 --> 01:22:28.765
What made you jump?


01:22:31.295 --> 01:22:33.205
Have you already met Dad?


01:22:33.375 --> 01:22:35.455
- Yes.
- How was it?


01:22:36.455 --> 01:22:37.535
He was scared.


01:22:39.545 --> 01:22:42.835
For his daughter, his home.
And I understand him well.


01:22:46.375 --> 01:22:49.415
Don't worry, Lyuba, I'm
not going to marry him.


01:22:50.835 --> 01:22:53.665
So your blessings would be wasted.


01:22:54.335 --> 01:22:55.495
Well, too bad.


01:22:58.374 --> 01:23:01.494
Here comes Dad with his military convoy.


01:23:05.704 --> 01:23:06.704
Yulia!


01:23:08.744 --> 01:23:10.454
- Where is she?
- In her room.


01:23:10.624 --> 01:23:12.954
She's with a boy in there,
and I don't think that...


01:23:13.124 --> 01:23:14.664
Out of the way!


01:23:28.384 --> 01:23:30.504
It was so much better without you!


01:23:37.544 --> 01:23:39.284
Why are you doing this?


01:23:40.294 --> 01:23:41.284
What?


01:23:41.454 --> 01:23:43.024
Inhale. It hurts.


01:23:43.444 --> 01:23:45.244
And you give a fuck?


01:23:45.294 --> 01:23:49.034
We have a tradition. Every time
some superior race comes along


01:23:49.204 --> 01:23:51.624
to destroy humanity,
we all start to smoke,


01:23:51.784 --> 01:23:53.494
so we can croak faster.


01:23:53.664 --> 01:23:57.124
We don't want to destroy you,
you're hurting yourselves.


01:23:58.494 --> 01:24:01.034
I urgently need an
interpreter from space.


01:24:02.294 --> 01:24:04.244
<i>- Do you like it here?
- No, I don't like it.</i>


01:24:04.414 --> 01:24:06.584
<i>- And where do you like it?
- There, where the hill is.</i>


01:24:06.744 --> 01:24:08.454
<i>But I can't go there now.</i>


01:24:08.624 --> 01:24:11.834
<i>- Why, do you think?
- There's this thing.</i>


01:24:13.374 --> 01:24:15.454
<i>- Is it hard? I'll help you.
- Of course!</i>


01:24:15.874 --> 01:24:18.874
<i>You can't carry five litres.
That's why I take less.</i>


01:24:19.044 --> 01:24:21.204
<i>But the soup is hardly
cooked, I must go again.</i>


01:24:21.374 --> 01:24:23.034
<i>How, not too hard?
Of course, it's hard.</i>


01:24:23.204 --> 01:24:25.834
<i>That's so cool! Before,
no one was interested.</i>


01:24:25.994 --> 01:24:28.914
<i>Now, everyone's talking about us.
There are reporters everywhere!</i>


01:24:29.084 --> 01:24:30.334
<i>Throw the ball! Thanks.</i>


01:24:30.494 --> 01:24:35.373
<i>- Do you want it to be the same forever?
- Well, it won't always be. Probably...</i>


01:24:35.543 --> 01:24:38.953
<i>Because it's martial law. And this
isn't a request! You have to comply!</i>


01:24:39.123 --> 01:24:42.083
<i>Why are you standing here with
a rifle? Who are you guarding?</i>


01:24:42.243 --> 01:24:44.953
<i>- Difficult to answer?
- Should I take your phone away?</i>


01:24:45.123 --> 01:24:46.873
<i>We take pity on those who guard them.</i>


01:24:47.043 --> 01:24:49.953
<i>Give them money so they can be
comfortable here in the district!</i>


01:24:50.123 --> 01:24:51.413
Hi.


01:24:52.333 --> 01:24:54.583
Don't worry, we won't stay long.


01:24:54.743 --> 01:24:56.993
We need to change clothes.


01:24:56.993 --> 01:24:58.313
Don't worry.


01:24:59.043 --> 01:25:02.873
<i>They will kill you all, one by one.
Mark my words! You all!</i>


01:25:03.043 --> 01:25:04.703
<i>I'm not a politician.</i>


01:25:04.873 --> 01:25:07.993
<i>So I'll keep it simple.
I don't like what's going on.</i>


01:25:08.163 --> 01:25:09.243
<i>No one likes it.</i>


01:25:09.413 --> 01:25:12.583
<i>But we're not doing anything.
And what options do we have?</i>


01:25:12.743 --> 01:25:15.743
<i>We can run away or bear it all.</i>


01:25:15.913 --> 01:25:20.163
<i>Or we can stand up and say,
This is our Earth!</i>


01:25:20.663 --> 01:25:22.333
<i>This is our Earth!</i>


01:25:22.493 --> 01:25:24.033
<i>That's all I have to say.</i>


01:25:24.453 --> 01:25:26.163
<i>THIS IS OUR EARTH!</i>


01:25:28.333 --> 01:25:30.913
Listen, this is not all like that. No.


01:25:43.333 --> 01:25:46.903
- Where are your clothes?
- They're in there, in the closet.


01:25:53.083 --> 01:25:54.493
Take it off!


01:25:58.703 --> 01:26:00.163
Turn around.


01:26:05.623 --> 01:26:08.453
Me too? Turn around?


01:26:08.623 --> 01:26:09.993
- Away from me?
- Yeah.


01:26:11.332 --> 01:26:12.662
Try it.


01:26:17.912 --> 01:26:21.442
This is actually Dad's. Listen,
he'll be here in half an hour.


01:26:21.442 --> 01:26:24.402
Maybe you can hang
around in the subway?


01:26:24.542 --> 01:26:27.492
It's really crowded.
I mean, it would be safer.


01:26:27.662 --> 01:26:31.142
- Don't think I'm kicking you out.
- I have a better idea!


01:26:33.022 --> 01:26:37.022
Why does it hurt so much?


01:26:43.912 --> 01:26:45.122
How do you like it?


01:26:45.292 --> 01:26:47.872
Unusual, interesting, electric pulsation.


01:26:48.042 --> 01:26:49.242
Clearly!


01:26:49.412 --> 01:26:51.742
No one will look for us here.


01:26:51.912 --> 01:26:55.412
A concert during martial law.
How unlikely is that?


01:26:56.332 --> 01:26:58.982
- Let's rip it up?
- We'll rip ourselves apart?


01:27:22.702 --> 01:27:25.062
What are you standing
there for? Undress!


01:27:28.622 --> 01:27:30.492
Hi, Tyoma!


01:27:30.662 --> 01:27:33.282
Listen, last time,


01:27:33.452 --> 01:27:35.082
I was confused.


01:27:35.242 --> 01:27:36.832
You understand.


01:27:37.702 --> 01:27:40.412
No wait! I have some info!


01:27:44.582 --> 01:27:47.831
You're doing fine!
Almost like a human!


01:27:47.991 --> 01:27:51.331
I am a human. We're different
branches of the same tree!


01:27:51.491 --> 01:27:54.031
- I can't hear you!
- Give me your hand, you will.


01:27:55.411 --> 01:27:56.661
My hand?


01:28:00.491 --> 01:28:04.581
Shut up! Guess who I just saw!


01:28:50.951 --> 01:28:52.081
Where are we?


01:28:53.621 --> 01:28:55.531
This is my home.


01:28:56.041 --> 01:29:00.351
It's almost like yours, but here
death hasn't occurred for a long time.


01:29:00.871 --> 01:29:04.491
Do you often take girls home
on the very first date?


01:29:05.541 --> 01:29:06.911
You are the first.


01:29:07.741 --> 01:29:10.201
We're not allowed to make contact.


01:29:10.371 --> 01:29:12.161
Crashing at Chertanovo was not contact?


01:29:12.331 --> 01:29:14.241
We didn't want you to notice us.


01:29:14.411 --> 01:29:17.991
The ship hit a meteor shower,
and the cloaking device failed.


01:29:18.161 --> 01:29:20.781
- And then we knocked you down.
- Yes.


01:29:22.331 --> 01:29:26.370
If someone tries to get on
the ship, Saul will destroy it.


01:29:26.950 --> 01:29:30.620
We can't allow our technology
to fall into your hands.


01:29:30.780 --> 01:29:33.620
And you're all ready to die for this?


01:29:33.780 --> 01:29:34.980
It's...


01:29:35.920 --> 01:29:38.220
It's the protocol.


01:29:45.910 --> 01:29:48.780
So we return with your shilk.


01:29:48.950 --> 01:29:50.240
Then what?


01:29:52.540 --> 01:29:54.410
Then we fly away.


01:29:56.660 --> 01:29:57.910
Forever?


01:30:03.620 --> 01:30:04.870
People!


01:30:05.950 --> 01:30:09.200
It's the curfew. We need to end.


01:30:09.370 --> 01:30:13.990
<i>But I want you to know. Many
of you have lost loved ones.</i>


01:30:14.160 --> 01:30:16.740
<i>Many of you crave revenge.</i>


01:30:16.910 --> 01:30:18.080
It's here.


01:30:18.240 --> 01:30:20.740
<i>Stay united!</i>


01:30:20.910 --> 01:30:23.120
<i>It's important, especially today!</i>


01:30:48.950 --> 01:30:51.330
Well, that's it?


01:30:56.540 --> 01:30:59.120
This is harmful. Remember?


01:31:00.040 --> 01:31:02.449
I just wanted to understand.
What it's like.


01:31:02.619 --> 01:31:04.449
When you smoke?


01:31:05.239 --> 01:31:06.529
When you die.


01:31:12.449 --> 01:31:14.629
You don't give a fuck, do you?


01:31:37.659 --> 01:31:38.829
Right then.


01:31:39.539 --> 01:31:40.529
Go.


01:31:56.779 --> 01:31:59.619
<i>- Yes?
- How are you? Can we meet?</i>


01:32:05.039 --> 01:32:06.739
Tyoma, I can't.


01:32:09.619 --> 01:32:11.659
Or, well. I don't want to.


01:32:11.829 --> 01:32:14.779
Listen, you're a great guy. I just...


01:32:15.239 --> 01:32:21.159
<i>Yes, yes, I'm awesome, I know.
But obviously not awesome enough.</i>


01:32:21.329 --> 01:32:24.779
<i>But, never mind. Don't
worry. Everything's fine.</i>


01:32:27.489 --> 01:32:28.159
<i>Yes?</i>


01:32:28.159 --> 01:32:30.199
<i>Of course. I understand everything.</i>


01:32:30.369 --> 01:32:31.829
<i>I'm not stupid.</i>


01:32:33.039 --> 01:32:34.949
<i>You love him, don't you?</i>


01:32:35.119 --> 01:32:36.199
<i>Yes?</i>


01:32:39.748 --> 01:32:40.748
Yes.


01:32:41.538 --> 01:32:43.158
<i>Very well.</i>


01:32:58.658 --> 01:33:00.618
- I'll explain everything.
- No!


01:33:01.328 --> 01:33:02.738
Don't, Tyoma!


01:33:02.908 --> 01:33:04.278
- Don't do this, please!
- Rus!


01:33:04.448 --> 01:33:05.448
What?


01:33:05.618 --> 01:33:07.578
She asked you not to do this.


01:33:11.038 --> 01:33:13.328
- I'll do it myself.
- No!


01:33:13.488 --> 01:33:15.278
- Let him go!
- Quiet! Quiet!


01:33:15.448 --> 01:33:17.278
- Take your hands off me!
- Don't shout!


01:33:18.158 --> 01:33:19.328
Stand up!


01:33:24.288 --> 01:33:25.408
Tyoma, don't!


01:33:27.618 --> 01:33:29.658
- Be quiet!
- No!


01:33:29.828 --> 01:33:31.948
Please stop!


01:33:37.908 --> 01:33:39.368
Quiet, quiet!


01:33:40.198 --> 01:33:42.408
I always knew you weren't
like everyone else.


01:33:42.578 --> 01:33:43.778
Quiet, quiet, quiet.


01:33:51.238 --> 01:33:52.158
No!


01:33:52.328 --> 01:33:53.778
Quiet. Don't shout.


01:33:55.948 --> 01:33:58.618
I tried to understand
what do you even need, eh?


01:33:59.448 --> 01:34:01.368
What more could I do for you?


01:34:04.198 --> 01:34:05.868
Please let him go!


01:34:06.038 --> 01:34:07.238
No!


01:34:07.618 --> 01:34:08.908
Will you shut up?!


01:34:10.158 --> 01:34:12.198
And you don't even need anything.


01:34:14.657 --> 01:34:16.867
You just dumped me.


01:34:18.907 --> 01:34:20.117
Bitch.


01:34:21.157 --> 01:34:22.327
Tyoma!


01:34:24.697 --> 01:34:27.077
- Look at me!
- He's not a human!


01:34:27.237 --> 01:34:28.527
Tyoma!


01:34:29.287 --> 01:34:30.277
What's this?


01:34:31.777 --> 01:34:33.617
Check it out.


01:34:35.537 --> 01:34:36.827
Tyoma, he's not a human!


01:34:39.287 --> 01:34:41.987
Give them that thing back
and they'll fly away, please!


01:34:42.157 --> 01:34:43.737
They just want to fly away!


01:34:50.737 --> 01:34:52.617
Not a human, you say?


01:34:54.327 --> 01:34:57.987
They're not like we thought.
They're better than us, Tyoma.


01:34:59.657 --> 01:35:00.697
Better?


01:35:08.287 --> 01:35:11.407
Where are you from? Another galaxy?


01:35:11.577 --> 01:35:13.117
From this one.


01:35:13.287 --> 01:35:14.947
The constellation of Gemini.


01:35:18.327 --> 01:35:20.077
And we are from Chertanovo.


01:35:23.537 --> 01:35:25.487
Is he even better than me?


01:36:24.866 --> 01:36:26.026
Rus!


01:36:28.986 --> 01:36:30.906
Breathe! Rus!


01:36:32.906 --> 01:36:34.276
Tyoma, the patrol!


01:36:47.696 --> 01:36:48.696
Help him!


01:36:48.866 --> 01:36:50.366
Help him!


01:36:50.536 --> 01:36:52.976
Shilk can't resurrect the dead.


01:36:55.986 --> 01:36:58.656
Don't move! Hands up
where I can see them!


01:37:09.486 --> 01:37:11.736
Tyoma, what should we do now?


01:37:12.696 --> 01:37:14.616
Gather everyone together!


01:37:14.776 --> 01:37:16.326
Yes. Everyone?


01:37:17.156 --> 01:37:18.196
Everyone!


01:37:20.236 --> 01:37:22.236
These creatures killed Rus.


01:37:25.036 --> 01:37:26.335
Well, that's it.


01:37:29.285 --> 01:37:30.285
Yeah.


01:37:48.405 --> 01:37:50.365
THEY KILLED A HUMAN!


01:37:50.385 --> 01:37:52.685
Let's all meet in an hour!


01:38:03.575 --> 01:38:06.655
Look, everybody's going.
Let's go too.


01:38:12.955 --> 01:38:14.155
THEY KILLED A HUMAN!


01:38:21.325 --> 01:38:23.325
This is our Earth!


01:38:23.825 --> 01:38:25.695
This is our Earth!


01:38:29.825 --> 01:38:31.575
<i>Dear passengers...</i>


01:38:36.365 --> 01:38:37.985
This is our Earth!


01:38:41.005 --> 01:38:43.005
THIS IS OUR EARTH!


01:38:50.945 --> 01:38:53.615
Rus and I went to the
same kindergarten.


01:38:54.445 --> 01:38:56.235
Our whole life together!


01:39:00.945 --> 01:39:03.444
Once we were sent
together to a camp.


01:39:05.194 --> 01:39:07.234
We were 10 years old, and so small.


01:39:07.404 --> 01:39:09.444
There was a mountain
stream, a steep slope.


01:39:09.864 --> 01:39:11.984
Everyone was afraid to jump.


01:39:12.484 --> 01:39:15.364
Well, I decided to
show off for the girls.


01:39:16.574 --> 01:39:18.524
I took off and jumped.


01:39:21.324 --> 01:39:23.484
There was a strong current.


01:39:23.654 --> 01:39:27.024
I was immediately carried away.
My legs cramped from the cold.


01:39:27.194 --> 01:39:29.734
And Rus jumped after me.


01:39:31.864 --> 01:39:35.484
He couldn't swim to save his
life, but he still jumped.


01:39:35.654 --> 01:39:37.234
To save me!


01:39:38.864 --> 01:39:41.614
Fuck knows what was going on in his head.


01:39:43.074 --> 01:39:45.194
He didn't really think
about it at all.


01:39:46.984 --> 01:39:48.824
You knew Rus.


01:39:50.824 --> 01:39:53.444
In the end, I had to get him out.


01:39:54.114 --> 01:39:56.444
We laughed about it for days.


01:39:57.574 --> 01:39:59.404
And today I've lost him.


01:40:06.194 --> 01:40:08.774
Many of you have lost
their loved ones.


01:40:08.944 --> 01:40:10.594
My brother's cousin.


01:40:11.044 --> 01:40:12.444
My son's in hospital.


01:40:12.444 --> 01:40:16.234
Slava Porogov, from the 9th
floor, is still missing.


01:40:16.324 --> 01:40:18.984
And what did they do in the end?


01:40:19.154 --> 01:40:21.114
Erect a fence!


01:40:22.114 --> 01:40:24.324
Deploy barbed wire!


01:40:25.364 --> 01:40:28.074
Soldiers with machine guns!


01:40:28.614 --> 01:40:32.074
To protect them, not us!


01:40:32.984 --> 01:40:36.064
- They have their orders.
- The hell with them!


01:40:36.284 --> 01:40:37.944
They have their orders.


01:40:38.654 --> 01:40:40.023
Yeah?


01:40:42.823 --> 01:40:45.103
Can't we re-establish order ourselves?


01:40:45.103 --> 01:40:46.853
Yes we can!


01:40:46.983 --> 01:40:48.733
Or do you prefer to go home?


01:40:48.903 --> 01:40:49.863
No!


01:40:50.033 --> 01:40:52.403
And wait until someone else is killed!


01:40:52.573 --> 01:40:53.273
No!


01:40:53.443 --> 01:40:55.193
Are you satisfied with waiting?


01:40:55.363 --> 01:40:56.863
No!


01:40:59.443 --> 01:41:00.693
And remember.


01:41:01.573 --> 01:41:03.863
We didn't attack anyone.


01:41:04.863 --> 01:41:06.923
We didn't invite anyone either!


01:41:06.983 --> 01:41:08.863
Yes!


01:41:09.483 --> 01:41:11.323
This is our Earth!


01:41:11.483 --> 01:41:13.023
This is our Earth!


01:41:13.033 --> 01:41:16.703
This. Our. Earth!!!


01:41:16.703 --> 01:41:18.163
This is our Earth!


01:41:18.323 --> 01:41:21.483
This is our Earth!


01:41:33.403 --> 01:41:36.073
- Please, wait!
- Out of the way!


01:41:36.233 --> 01:41:38.233
Where are you going?


01:41:38.403 --> 01:41:39.943
This is our Earth!


01:41:40.113 --> 01:41:41.523
I beg you!


01:41:42.323 --> 01:41:46.123
Please! We're human beings!
We don't have the right to kill!


01:41:47.773 --> 01:41:49.443
We're human beings!


01:42:05.403 --> 01:42:07.653
Give me the key to the garage!


01:42:10.113 --> 01:42:12.423
- You take the car, Pyth.
- Where are you going?


01:42:12.433 --> 01:42:13.453
I'll catch up.


01:42:13.453 --> 01:42:14.563
Where are you going?


01:42:14.563 --> 01:42:15.562
Tyoma!


01:42:22.242 --> 01:42:23.242
Time's running out.


01:42:23.282 --> 01:42:25.722
I can stop everything,
but you need to let us go.


01:42:25.722 --> 01:42:28.642
- Don't you understand?
- It's pointless.


01:42:28.772 --> 01:42:30.152
They have their orders.


01:42:30.322 --> 01:42:33.342
They were told to
guard us, so they will.


01:42:35.482 --> 01:42:38.652
It's your bad luck. You should
have crashed in Finland.


01:42:38.822 --> 01:42:40.652
Be quiet and sit still!


01:42:41.322 --> 01:42:44.052
Forgive me, it shouldn't
have been like this.


01:42:44.732 --> 01:42:46.572
We shouldn't have come here.


01:42:54.992 --> 01:42:56.032
Do you regret it?


01:42:56.032 --> 01:42:58.732
Was I not clear enough?
Stop talking!


01:42:58.732 --> 01:43:00.022
Let them.


01:43:31.282 --> 01:43:36.632
This is our Earth!
This is our Earth! This is our Earth!


01:43:36.692 --> 01:43:39.732
- Here we come!
- This is our Earth!


01:43:47.232 --> 01:43:49.692
First to Twelfth, First to Twelfth.


01:43:49.862 --> 01:43:51.362
We have people here.


01:43:51.901 --> 01:43:52.941
Many people!


01:43:57.321 --> 01:43:58.651
Citizens!


01:43:58.821 --> 01:44:01.401
Disperse immediately!
This is a restricted area!


01:44:02.861 --> 01:44:04.731
Citizens! Disperse immediately!


01:44:04.901 --> 01:44:05.901
Here we go!


01:44:08.151 --> 01:44:11.691
Disperse immediately!
This is restricted area!


01:44:12.531 --> 01:44:13.981
Disperse!


01:44:25.821 --> 01:44:27.361
Sergei Ivanovich!


01:44:28.531 --> 01:44:29.771
That's OK. Go on.


01:44:32.361 --> 01:44:33.981
Yes? Speak!


01:44:36.151 --> 01:44:37.571
How many?!


01:44:39.231 --> 01:44:40.981
Get me Lebedev.


01:44:43.071 --> 01:44:46.401
What are you looking at, eh?
What are you looking at me for?


01:44:58.731 --> 01:45:03.191
Stop! That's an order!
Stop immediately!


01:45:07.821 --> 01:45:09.941
Do not move!


01:45:16.821 --> 01:45:18.271
Which side are you on?


01:45:18.441 --> 01:45:21.321
Citizens! Immediately
cease any illegal action!


01:45:21.481 --> 01:45:23.441
Your actions are illegal!


01:45:23.611 --> 01:45:24.821
Forward!


01:45:24.981 --> 01:45:28.570
Disperse! Otherwise we'll
have to use force against you.


01:45:46.400 --> 01:45:47.770
Let's go!!!


01:45:49.030 --> 01:45:50.480
Close ranks!


01:45:54.320 --> 01:45:56.190
Closer!


01:45:58.400 --> 01:46:03.440
The right flank, closer!
Five steps forward!


01:46:04.980 --> 01:46:08.400
Five more steps forward!


01:46:21.610 --> 01:46:23.110
- Hands off me!
- Colonel!


01:46:23.280 --> 01:46:26.110
The body was handed over to the
experts. They also found this.


01:46:26.440 --> 01:46:27.480
Take them off!


01:46:29.150 --> 01:46:30.480
What did you do, Yul?


01:46:30.650 --> 01:46:32.370
Me? What did you do?


01:46:32.430 --> 01:46:35.600
Security log, space
defence, missile defence...


01:46:35.600 --> 01:46:38.520
You're paranoid! You shot them down!


01:46:41.320 --> 01:46:42.570
And who are you?


01:46:42.730 --> 01:46:45.820
If you get closer, Saul
will blow up the ship!


01:46:45.980 --> 01:46:48.820
We'll all die, they and
we, you understand?


01:47:10.149 --> 01:47:12.859
Why do you believe him,
and not me?


01:47:13.029 --> 01:47:14.889
Because at least he talks to me.


01:47:14.889 --> 01:47:17.399
He's not a human! We
don't know who they are!


01:47:17.489 --> 01:47:19.409
Am I a human? Can you listen to me?


01:47:19.409 --> 01:47:22.919
Instead of bossing me around?
Why don't you try to understand me?


01:47:22.919 --> 01:47:25.049
- I'm trying to!
- Then give us a chance.


01:47:25.049 --> 01:47:27.429
We know what to do.


01:47:27.439 --> 01:47:28.439
Lebedev.


01:47:28.609 --> 01:47:30.859
Valentin, how serious is the situation?


01:47:32.859 --> 01:47:34.269
Good, listen.


01:47:34.439 --> 01:47:37.519
You are on the spot
so act as you think fit.


01:47:38.029 --> 01:47:42.019
I'll take full responsibility!
You have half an hour.


01:47:47.149 --> 01:47:50.129
What happens in half an hour?


01:47:52.859 --> 01:47:55.819
In half an hour, a new day begins.


01:47:56.109 --> 01:47:57.509
I hope so.


01:48:00.859 --> 01:48:02.479
Full assault readiness!


01:48:02.479 --> 01:48:04.809
You crazy?! You're
going to open fire?!


01:48:04.809 --> 01:48:05.809
You fool!


01:48:06.439 --> 01:48:08.859
Do you even understand
what's going on?!


01:48:11.149 --> 01:48:12.359
Yulia.


01:48:13.859 --> 01:48:16.319
Forgive me. I really want to help,


01:48:18.359 --> 01:48:20.729
but I've already had a loss,


01:48:22.109 --> 01:48:23.439
I'm afraid.


01:48:25.109 --> 01:48:27.109
So, Dad, it's up to me.


01:48:27.109 --> 01:48:27.819
Yulia!


01:48:27.819 --> 01:48:29.279
Get away from me!


01:48:30.529 --> 01:48:33.569
We'll all die. A minute sooner or later,
what's the difference?


01:48:35.189 --> 01:48:37.069
Dad. Just trust me, OK?


01:48:37.229 --> 01:48:39.189
Car keys, fast!


01:48:39.359 --> 01:48:41.438
- Go on!
- The keys!


01:48:44.858 --> 01:48:46.148
Follow me!


01:48:59.568 --> 01:49:01.648
- Tactical unit, here, now!
- Yes!


01:49:01.818 --> 01:49:02.818
Run!


01:49:12.108 --> 01:49:13.108
Out of the way!


01:49:33.108 --> 01:49:34.948
They're going to blow it up now?


01:49:34.948 --> 01:49:37.898
No, Saul's waiting.
He'll wait until the end.


01:49:38.438 --> 01:49:40.898
Colonel, may I ask a question?


01:49:41.068 --> 01:49:43.938
- Yes.
- Are we really going to open fire?


01:49:44.108 --> 01:49:46.148
- What was the order?
- Assault readiness.


01:49:46.318 --> 01:49:48.318
- Then get ready!
- Yes!


01:49:48.478 --> 01:49:50.818
- No assault whatsoever.
- Yes!


01:49:52.688 --> 01:49:54.568
Must give her time.


01:50:26.227 --> 01:50:27.357
Die!


01:50:30.107 --> 01:50:32.147
<i>We're following Tiger.</i>


01:50:33.067 --> 01:50:34.187
Shit!


01:52:27.606 --> 01:52:29.566
<i>Avoid collisions!</i>


01:53:36.685 --> 01:53:38.475
<i>Back to the vehicles!</i>


01:53:50.645 --> 01:53:52.765
<i>They attack people!</i>


01:53:53.685 --> 01:53:54.855
<i>We should retaliate!</i>


01:54:09.315 --> 01:54:10.475
I love you.


01:54:13.335 --> 01:54:14.915
<i>They seem to be retreating.</i>


01:54:15.145 --> 01:54:17.145
<i>Nobody moves. Just watch.</i>


01:54:48.105 --> 01:54:49.355
Yulia!


01:55:25.274 --> 01:55:26.264
Stop!


01:55:26.434 --> 01:55:28.254
Lower your weapons!


01:56:11.644 --> 01:56:13.314
What are you doing to her?


01:56:17.854 --> 01:56:20.354
What are you doing to her?!


01:56:28.104 --> 01:56:30.764
Water helps tissue regeneration.


01:56:30.934 --> 01:56:34.604
- Who am I talking to?!
- I am Saul, a small research vessel.


01:56:34.764 --> 01:56:36.764
You can talk to me.


01:56:39.764 --> 01:56:40.894
Will she...


01:56:45.403 --> 01:56:46.603
Will she live?


01:56:46.613 --> 01:56:50.013
Not for long. Seventy or
eighty Earth years.


01:56:54.433 --> 01:56:57.433
- And he?
- Hakon should have lived forever.


01:56:57.603 --> 01:56:59.973
But he passed on his life to her.


01:57:00.143 --> 01:57:02.563
This is not an exact translation.


01:57:03.273 --> 01:57:06.013
- Why did he do this?
- From my point of view,


01:57:06.183 --> 01:57:09.723
this was a chain of random events,
with extremely low probability.


01:57:09.893 --> 01:57:11.853
You call it fate.


01:57:12.183 --> 01:57:13.723
Did he come alone?


01:57:14.723 --> 01:57:17.853
- Where are the others?
- The others don't know he flew here.


01:57:18.023 --> 01:57:21.263
It is prohibited to visit your planet.


01:57:22.063 --> 01:57:24.763
- Why?
- Extremely aggressive social environment.


01:57:24.763 --> 01:57:27.423
Despite close to ideal climatic conditions,


01:57:27.563 --> 01:57:31.223
Four billion violent deaths
in the last 5,000 years.


01:57:31.393 --> 01:57:35.023
Over the same period, about
15,000 major military conflicts.


01:57:35.023 --> 01:57:38.383
The complete depletion of resources
and extinction of mankind


01:57:38.383 --> 01:57:40.263
is no more than 600 years away.


01:57:40.393 --> 01:57:43.383
As I see it, all you plan
to do is live forever, right?


01:57:43.383 --> 01:57:45.173
We want to observe.


01:57:45.763 --> 01:57:49.563
Contact with undeveloped civilizations
only accelerates their destruction.


01:57:49.723 --> 01:57:51.343
Hakon wanted to collect data,


01:57:51.343 --> 01:57:53.713
to prove that you were ready for contact.


01:57:53.853 --> 01:57:56.353
The results of the mission are negative.


01:57:56.973 --> 01:58:00.563
Then there'll be no further attempts?


01:58:01.523 --> 01:58:04.563
There is one factor that
could change the forecast.


01:58:04.723 --> 01:58:05.853
Which one?


01:58:07.023 --> 01:58:08.023
Her.


01:58:08.023 --> 01:58:10.713
Her decision doesn't lend
itself to analysis.


01:58:10.723 --> 01:58:13.053
I don't understand why she saved Hakon.


01:58:13.183 --> 01:58:16.223
And why Hakon decided that
she should live instead of him.


01:58:16.393 --> 01:58:18.263
This is not an exact translation.


01:58:18.263 --> 01:58:21.092
I will have to reconsider the
results of the mission.


01:58:21.222 --> 01:58:24.312
Our common future depends on this.


01:58:24.472 --> 01:58:27.972
I must share with the others
what Hakon found out.


01:58:28.062 --> 01:58:30.862
And that was... what?


01:58:30.862 --> 01:58:34.192
That perhaps there's something
more important than immortality.


01:58:34.392 --> 01:58:36.642
This is an exact translation.


02:00:20.651 --> 02:00:26.731
<i>Everyone is looking for a dream,
we're leaving home.</i>


02:00:27.811 --> 02:00:29.401
<i>To dive into the depths</i>


02:00:31.151 --> 02:00:36.521
<i>In a circle of strangers,
to fall down, and rise again,</i>


02:00:37.981 --> 02:00:43.441
<i>To strike out letters, to wish and to forgive.</i>


02:00:45.231 --> 02:00:50.561
<i>To weather our lips; we're losing ourselves</i>


02:00:51.361 --> 02:00:57.271
<i>Sitting in comfort, tired of being bored</i>


02:00:59.021 --> 02:01:04.651
<i>And missing the people on
the photos; I'm tired of being alone,</i>


02:01:05.111 --> 02:01:11.901
<i>Of being a non-melted
butter, but I'll hug you.</i>


02:01:12.111 --> 02:01:16.021
<i>I'm back, I'm happy.</i>


02:01:17.981 --> 02:01:20.561
<i>Open the windows wide.</i>


02:01:21.311 --> 02:01:23.901
<i>Wake me up with the wind.</i>


02:01:24.861 --> 02:01:25.861
<i>Let this city roar.</i>


02:01:28.231 --> 02:01:30.811
<i>Our meetings are so rare.</i>


02:01:31.651 --> 02:01:34.650
<i>Open the windows wide.</i>


02:01:35.110 --> 02:01:38.230
<i>Wake me up with the wind.</i>


02:01:38.770 --> 02:01:41.150
<i>Let this city roar.</i>


02:01:42.060 --> 02:01:44.730
<i>Our meetings are so rare.</i>


02:01:45.850 --> 02:01:47.820
They're still talking on TV


02:01:47.890 --> 02:01:50.560
about the heroic victory
over the aliens.


02:01:50.720 --> 02:01:54.180
And while the scientists are racking
their brains over the water engines,


02:01:54.350 --> 02:01:57.600
people are buying buckwheat,
preparing for the next invasion.


02:01:57.760 --> 02:02:00.010
No one notices the most important thing.


02:02:00.180 --> 02:02:07.890
One stranger, in the far distant cosmos,
believed in us more than we did ourselves.


02:02:11.060 --> 02:02:14.850
Many say that they won't be able
to live the way they did before.


02:02:17.850 --> 02:02:19.180
I...


02:02:20.720 --> 02:02:22.640
...won't for sure.

